window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b089-739407dbcc0b3235.json"]={sha256:"739407dbcc0b32353d6854caea51d8c061a6fd2b4bafbcb590daa21ce0518f47",value:{"id":"b089","title":"雙層通風幕牆整合","titleEn":"Double-skin ventilated facade integration","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"從雙層通風幕牆的腔體類型與氣候條件出發，建立日射吸熱與通風量決定腔體溫升、煙囪效應決定浮力風量的模型，說明外層玻璃與懸挑托架、檢修走道的結構設計、開口與遮陽的細部，再處理施工整合、控制系統試運轉、樣品牆熱流量測與腔體煙控，最後以清潔、結露與實測能耗完成交接，並以柏林 GSW 總部、溫尼伯曼尼托巴水電大樓與倫敦聖瑪莉斧街 30 號說明不同的腔體策略。","summaryEn":"Starting from cavity types and climate, build models in which absorbed solar gain and airflow set cavity temperature rise and the stack effect sets buoyant airflow, explain the structural design of outer glass, cantilever brackets and maintenance walkways and the detailing of openings and shading, then cover construction integration, control commissioning, mock-up heat-flow measurement and smoke control in the cavity, and close with cleaning, condensation and measured energy at handover, comparing cavity strategies at the GSW headquarters in Berlin, Manitoba Hydro Place in Winnipeg and 30 St Mary Axe in London.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-facade-digital","subcategoryTitle":"帷幕牆、垂直運輸與數位營建","subcategoryTitleEn":"Facades, vertical transport and digital construction","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-facade-digital","learningTags":["structures","st-facade-digital","facade"],"architectureFamily":"facade","architectureNodes":[["外層單層玻璃","Outer single glazing"],["通風腔體與遮陽","Ventilated cavity and shading"],["內層隔熱帷幕牆","Inner insulated curtain wall"],["托架與檢修走道","Brackets and maintenance walkway"],["風門與自動控制","Dampers and automatic controls"],["防火分隔與煙控","Fire divisions and smoke control"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[0,3],[3,2],[1,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"facade","labels":["外層單層玻璃","通風腔體與遮陽","內層隔熱帷幕牆","托架與檢修走道","風門與自動控制"],"labelsEn":["Outer single glazing","Ventilated cavity and shading","Inner insulated curtain wall","Brackets and maintenance walkway","Dampers and automatic controls"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：某 20 m 高的多樓層式雙層幕牆開間寬 3.0 m、層高 3.6 m、腔深 0.9 m。夏季晴天百葉吸收 0.5×600×10.8 = 3,240 W/開間，70% 即 2,268 W 進入腔體空氣。若以腔體出風溫升 ΔT ≤ 8 K 為目標，需風量 V = 2,268/(1,206×8) ≈ 0.235 m³/s。浮力壓差 ΔP = 1.2×9.81×20×8/300 ≈ 6.3 Pa；有效開口 Cd·A = V/√(2ΔP/ρ) = 0.235/3.24 ≈ 0.073 m²，以 50% 自由面積、Cd = 0.6 的百葉需毛面積約 0.073/0.3 ≈ 0.24 m²，加防蟲網（再乘 0.6）約 0.40 m²。外層托架根部彎矩約 2.65 kN·m。若腔體高度降為 10 m，ΔP 減半為約 3.1 Pa，同樣風量需開口增為約 √2 ≈ 1.41 倍，即約 0.57 m²。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實際建築的設計。","textEn":"Design exercise: a 20 m high multi-storey double-skin façade has 3.0 m bays, 3.6 m storeys and a 0.9 m cavity. On a clear summer day the blinds absorb 0.5×600×10.8 = 3,240 W per bay, 70% of which, 2,268 W, enters the cavity air. To keep the outlet temperature rise to ΔT ≤ 8 K requires V = 2,268/(1,206×8) ≈ 0.235 m³/s. The stack pressure is ΔP = 1.2×9.81×20×8/300 ≈ 6.3 Pa, so the effective opening is Cd·A = V/√(2ΔP/ρ) = 0.235/3.24 ≈ 0.073 m²; a louvre with 50% free area and Cd = 0.6 needs a gross area of about 0.073/0.3 ≈ 0.24 m², or about 0.40 m² with an insect screen (a further factor of 0.6). The outer-skin bracket root moment is about 2.65 kN·m. If the cavity height drops to 10 m, ΔP halves to about 3.1 Pa and the same airflow needs openings about √2 ≈ 1.41 times larger, about 0.57 m². Values are teaching assumptions, not the design of any real building.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b089-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「腔體類型與日射熱平衡」與「煙囪效應、風壓與腔體通風量」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cavity types and the solar heat balance\" and \"Stack effect, wind pressure and cavity airflow\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b089-v13-01","title":"腔體類型與日射熱平衡：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Cavity types and the solar heat balance: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「通風腔體熱平衡」如何影響雙層通風幕牆整合的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cavity heat balance” governs force, deformation or durability in “Double-skin ventilated facade integration”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"雙層幕牆在內層隔熱玻璃外再加一層單層玻璃，兩層之間形成數十公分到一公尺以上的通風腔體，常依分隔方式分為箱窗式、井箱式、走廊式與多樓層式。遮陽百葉放在腔體內可免受風雨，但百葉吸收的日射會加熱腔體空氣，若通風不足，腔體可能比室外熱得多，反而把熱推進室內。因此腔體的核心是熱平衡：吸收的日射熱必須由流經腔體的空氣帶走，風量與開口決定了腔體是「緩衝區」還是「烤箱」。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「通風腔體熱平衡」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A double-skin façade adds a single-glazed outer layer outside the insulated inner glazing, forming a ventilated cavity from a few tenths of a metre to over a metre deep, usually classified by its subdivision as box-window, shaft-box, corridor or multi-storey. Blinds in the cavity are protected from wind and rain, but the solar energy they absorb heats the cavity air, and with too little ventilation the cavity can become much hotter than outdoors and push heat indoors. The core of the cavity is therefore its heat balance: absorbed solar gain must be carried away by air flowing through the cavity, and airflow and openings decide whether the cavity is a buffer or an oven. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Cavity heat balance” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：百葉吸收率 0.5、垂直日射 600 W/m²，每格 3.0×3.6 = 10.8 m² 吸熱 0.5×600×10.8 = 3,240 W，其中 70% 對流入腔體空氣為 2,268 W。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With blind absorptance 0.5 and 600 W/m² vertical irradiance, each 3.0×3.6 = 10.8 m² bay absorbs 0.5×600×10.8 = 3,240 W, of which 70%, 2,268 W, is convected to cavity air.","failure":"常見誤解：「多加一層玻璃一定能減少建築的空調耗能。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding a second layer of glass always reduces air-conditioning energy.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「通風腔體熱平衡」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Cavity heat balance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-01-k1","title":"腔體類型與日射熱平衡","titleEn":"Cavity types and the solar heat balance","text":"雙層幕牆在內層隔熱玻璃外再加一層單層玻璃，兩層之間形成數十公分到一公尺以上的通風腔體，常依分隔方式分為箱窗式、井箱式、走廊式與多樓層式。遮陽百葉放在腔體內可免受風雨，但百葉吸收的日射會加熱腔體空氣，若通風不足，腔體可能比室外熱得多，反而把熱推進室內。","textEn":"A double-skin façade adds a single-glazed outer layer outside the insulated inner glazing, forming a ventilated cavity from a few tenths of a metre to over a metre deep, usually classified by its subdivision as box-window, shaft-box, corridor or multi-storey. Blinds in the cavity are protected from wind and rain, but the solar energy they absorb heats the cavity air, and with too little ventilation the cavity can become much hotter than outdoors and push heat indoors.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：多加一層玻璃一定能減少建築的空調耗能。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding a second layer of glass always reduces air-conditioning energy. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「腔體類型與日射熱平衡」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cavity types and the solar heat balance\" is correct?","options":["多加一層玻璃一定能減少建築的空調耗能。","雙層幕牆在內層隔熱玻璃外再加一層單層玻璃，兩層之間形成數十公分到一公尺以上的通風腔體，常依分隔方式分為箱窗式、井箱式、走廊式與多樓層式。","雙層幕牆的腔體只要夠高，空氣就一定會由下往上流動。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a second layer of glass always reduces air-conditioning energy.","A double-skin façade adds a single-glazed outer layer outside the insulated inner glazing, forming a ventilated cavity from a few tenths of a metre to over a metre deep, usually classified by its subdivision as box-window, shaft-box, corridor or multi-storey.","If the cavity is tall enough, air will always flow upward through it."],"answer":1,"explanation":"雙層幕牆在內層隔熱玻璃外再加一層單層玻璃，兩層之間形成數十公分到一公尺以上的通風腔體，常依分隔方式分為箱窗式、井箱式、走廊式與多樓層式。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A double-skin façade adds a single-glazed outer layer outside the insulated inner glazing, forming a ventilated cavity from a few tenths of a metre to over a metre deep, usually classified by its subdivision as box-window, shaft-box, corridor or multi-storey. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b089-v13-02","title":"腔體類型與日射熱平衡：定量估算","titleEn":"Cavity types and the solar heat balance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「通風腔體熱平衡」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cavity heat balance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：百葉吸收率 0.5、垂直日射 600 W/m²，每格 3.0×3.6 = 10.8 m² 吸熱 0.5×600×10.8 = 3,240 W，其中 70% 對流入腔體空氣為 2,268 W。腔體溫升 ΔT = Q/(ρ·cp·V)，ρ·cp = 1.2×1,005 ≈ 1,206 J/m³K：風量 0.3 m³/s 時 ΔT ≈ 6.3 K；風量降為 0.1 m³/s 時 ΔT ≈ 18.8 K。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With blind absorptance 0.5 and 600 W/m² vertical irradiance, each 3.0×3.6 = 10.8 m² bay absorbs 0.5×600×10.8 = 3,240 W, of which 70%, 2,268 W, is convected to cavity air. Temperature rise ΔT = Q/(ρ·cp·V) with ρ·cp = 1.2×1,005 ≈ 1,206 J/m³K: at 0.3 m³/s ΔT ≈ 6.3 K; if airflow drops to 0.1 m³/s, ΔT ≈ 18.8 K. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以分區熱網路模型或計算流體力學模擬各方位、季節與遮陽位置下的腔體溫度與內層玻璃熱流，檢查夏季最熱時段的腔體溫度上限與冬季的預熱效益；模擬假設須在樣品牆量測中驗證，並由機電與帷幕牆顧問共同確認。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Simulate cavity temperatures and heat flow through the inner glazing for each orientation, season and blind position with a zonal thermal-network model or computational fluid dynamics, checking the cavity temperature ceiling in the hottest summer hours and the preheating benefit in winter; the assumptions must be validated by mock-up measurement and agreed by the MEP and façade consultants.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"百葉吸收率 0.5、垂直日射 600 W/m²，每格 3.0×3.6 = 10.8 m² 吸熱 0.5×600×10.8 = 3,240 W，其中 70% 對流入腔體空氣為 2,268 W。腔體溫升 ΔT = Q/(ρ·cp·V)，ρ·cp = 1.2×1,005 ≈ 1,206 J/m³K：風量 0.3 m³/s 時 ΔT ≈ 6.3 K；風量降為 0.1 m³/s 時 ΔT ≈ 18.8 K。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"With blind absorptance 0.5 and 600 W/m² vertical irradiance, each 3.0×3.6 = 10.8 m² bay absorbs 0.5×600×10.8 = 3,240 W, of which 70%, 2,268 W, is convected to cavity air. Temperature rise ΔT = Q/(ρ·cp·V) with ρ·cp = 1.2×1,005 ≈ 1,206 J/m³K: at 0.3 m³/s ΔT ≈ 6.3 K; if airflow drops to 0.1 m³/s, ΔT ≈ 18.8 K. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「腔體類型與日射熱平衡」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cavity types and the solar heat balance\", which statement holds?","options":["腔體開口只要外觀上夠大，通風量就足夠。","雙層幕牆是被動式設計，完工後不需要控制系統試運轉。","百葉吸收率 0.5、垂直日射 600 W/m²，每格 3.0×3.6 = 10.8 m² 吸熱 0.5×600×10.8 = 3,240 W，其中 70% 對流入腔體空氣為 2,268 W。"],"optionsEn":["If cavity openings look large enough, the airflow will be sufficient.","A double-skin façade is passive, so it needs no control commissioning after completion.","With blind absorptance 0.5 and 600 W/m² vertical irradiance, each 3.0×3.6 = 10.8 m² bay absorbs 0.5×600×10.8 = 3,240 W, of which 70%, 2,268 W, is convected to cavity air."],"answer":2,"explanation":"百葉吸收率 0.5、垂直日射 600 W/m²，每格 3.0×3.6 = 10.8 m² 吸熱 0.5×600×10.8 = 3,240 W，其中 70% 對流入腔體空氣為 2,268 W。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With blind absorptance 0.5 and 600 W/m² vertical irradiance, each 3.0×3.6 = 10.8 m² bay absorbs 0.5×600×10.8 = 3,240 W, of which 70%, 2,268 W, is convected to cavity air. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b089-v13-03","title":"腔體類型與日射熱平衡：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cavity types and the solar heat balance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「通風腔體熱平衡」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cavity heat balance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以分區熱網路模型或計算流體力學模擬各方位、季節與遮陽位置下的腔體溫度與內層玻璃熱流，檢查夏季最熱時段的腔體溫度上限與冬季的預熱效益；模擬假設須在樣品牆量測中驗證，並由機電與帷幕牆顧問共同確認。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Simulate cavity temperatures and heat flow through the inner glazing for each orientation, season and blind position with a zonal thermal-network model or computational fluid dynamics, checking the cavity temperature ceiling in the hottest summer hours and the preheating benefit in winter; the assumptions must be validated by mock-up measurement and agreed by the MEP and façade consultants. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：方案階段就以當地氣候資料比較單層高性能帷幕牆與各類雙層幕牆的全年耗能、舒適度與造價，並把腔體最高溫度、最小風量與遮陽控制邏輯寫成設計準則，作為後續各專業共同遵守的目標。","observationEn":"Site practice: At concept stage compare annual energy, comfort and cost of a high-performance single skin against each double-skin type using local climate data, and write the maximum cavity temperature, minimum airflow and shading control logic into design criteria that all disciplines then follow.","failure":"注意干擾：在高日射地區採用封閉或通風不足的腔體，夏季腔體溫度遠高於室外，內層玻璃與窗框成為大型輻射熱源，空調負荷不降反升；百葉卡在放下位置又無法通風時，腔體高溫甚至使密封材料老化與玻璃熱破裂。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using a closed or under-ventilated cavity in a high-irradiance climate makes summer cavity temperatures far exceed outdoor air, so the inner glazing and frames become large radiant heat sources and cooling loads rise instead of falling; with blinds stuck down and ventilation blocked, cavity heat can even age seals and cause thermal breakage of glass. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以分區熱網路模型或計算流體力學模擬各方位、季節與遮陽位置下的腔體溫度與內層玻璃熱流，檢查夏季最熱時段的腔體溫度上限與冬季的預熱效益；模擬假設須在樣品牆量測中驗證，並由機電與帷幕牆顧問共同確認。","textEn":"Simulate cavity temperatures and heat flow through the inner glazing for each orientation, season and blind position with a zonal thermal-network model or computational fluid dynamics, checking the cavity temperature ceiling in the hottest summer hours and the preheating benefit in winter; the assumptions must be validated by mock-up measurement and agreed by the MEP and façade consultants.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"方案階段就以當地氣候資料比較單層高性能帷幕牆與各類雙層幕牆的全年耗能、舒適度與造價，並把腔體最高溫度、最小風量與遮陽控制邏輯寫成設計準則，作為後續各專業共同遵守的目標。","textEn":"At concept stage compare annual energy, comfort and cost of a high-performance single skin against each double-skin type using local climate data, and write the maximum cavity temperature, minimum airflow and shading control logic into design criteria that all disciplines then follow.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「腔體類型與日射熱平衡」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cavity types and the solar heat balance\"?","options":["以分區熱網路模型或計算流體力學模擬各方位、季節與遮陽位置下的腔體溫度與內層玻璃熱流，檢查夏季最熱時段的腔體溫度上限與冬季的預熱效益。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","雙層幕牆的外層玻璃可以擋住火焰，所以腔體不需要防火設計。"],"optionsEn":["Simulate cavity temperatures and heat flow through the inner glazing for each orientation, season and blind position with a zonal thermal-network model or computational fluid dynamics, checking the cavity temperature ceiling in the hottest summer hours and the preheating benefit in winter.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The outer glass of a double skin stops flames, so the cavity needs no fire design."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以分區熱網路模型或計算流體力學模擬各方位、季節與遮陽位置下的腔體溫度與內層玻璃熱流，檢查夏季最熱時段的腔體溫度上限與冬季的預熱效益；模擬假設須在樣品牆量測中驗證，並由機電與帷幕牆顧問共同確認。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Simulate cavity temperatures and heat flow through the inner glazing for each orientation, season and blind position with a zonal thermal-network model or computational fluid dynamics, checking the cavity temperature ceiling in the hottest summer hours and the preheating benefit in winter; the assumptions must be validated by mock-up measurement and agreed by the MEP and façade consultants. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b089-v13-04","title":"腔體類型與日射熱平衡：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cavity types and the solar heat balance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「通風腔體熱平衡」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cavity heat balance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"在高日射地區採用封閉或通風不足的腔體，夏季腔體溫度遠高於室外，內層玻璃與窗框成為大型輻射熱源，空調負荷不降反升；百葉卡在放下位置又無法通風時，腔體高溫甚至使密封材料老化與玻璃熱破裂。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using a closed or under-ventilated cavity in a high-irradiance climate makes summer cavity temperatures far exceed outdoor air, so the inner glazing and frames become large radiant heat sources and cooling loads rise instead of falling; with blinds stuck down and ventilation blocked, cavity heat can even age seals and cause thermal breakage of glass. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此腔體的核心是熱平衡：吸收的日射熱必須由流經腔體的空氣帶走，風量與開口決定了腔體是「緩衝區」還是「烤箱」。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The core of the cavity is therefore its heat balance: absorbed solar gain must be carried away by air flowing through the cavity, and airflow and openings decide whether the cavity is a buffer or an oven.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「多加一層玻璃一定能減少建築的空調耗能。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding a second layer of glass always reduces air-conditioning energy.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"在高日射地區採用封閉或通風不足的腔體，夏季腔體溫度遠高於室外，內層玻璃與窗框成為大型輻射熱源，空調負荷不降反升；百葉卡在放下位置又無法通風時，腔體高溫甚至使密封材料老化與玻璃熱破裂。","textEn":"Using a closed or under-ventilated cavity in a high-irradiance climate makes summer cavity temperatures far exceed outdoor air, so the inner glazing and frames become large radiant heat sources and cooling loads rise instead of falling; with blinds stuck down and ventilation blocked, cavity heat can even age seals and cause thermal breakage of glass.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「腔體類型與日射熱平衡」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cavity types and the solar heat balance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","在高日射地區採用封閉或通風不足的腔體，夏季腔體溫度遠高於室外，內層玻璃與窗框成為大型輻射熱源，空調負荷不降反升。","雙層幕牆的腔體只要夠高，空氣就一定會由下往上流動。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Using a closed or under-ventilated cavity in a high-irradiance climate makes summer cavity temperatures far exceed outdoor air, so the inner glazing and frames become large radiant heat sources and cooling loads rise instead of falling.","If the cavity is tall enough, air will always flow upward through it."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在高日射地區採用封閉或通風不足的腔體，夏季腔體溫度遠高於室外，內層玻璃與窗框成為大型輻射熱源，空調負荷不降反升；百葉卡在放下位置又無法通風時，腔體高溫甚至使密封材料老化與玻璃熱破裂。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using a closed or under-ventilated cavity in a high-irradiance climate makes summer cavity temperatures far exceed outdoor air, so the inner glazing and frames become large radiant heat sources and cooling loads rise instead of falling; with blinds stuck down and ventilation blocked, cavity heat can even age seals and cause thermal breakage of glass. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b089-v13-05","title":"煙囪效應、風壓與腔體通風量：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Stack effect, wind pressure and cavity airflow: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「煙囪效應浮力風量」如何影響雙層通風幕牆整合的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Stack-driven airflow” governs force, deformation or durability in “Double-skin ventilated facade integration”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"腔體空氣受熱後密度降低而上升，形成煙囪效應：腔體越高、溫差越大，浮力驅動的壓差就越大。多樓層式腔體可利用數十公尺的高度產生可觀的自然通風，柏林 GSW 總部的西向雙層立面即把腔體當成對流井，輔助高層辦公室的自然通風。然而外部風壓同樣作用在進出風口上，迎風面可能加強、背風面可能抵銷甚至逆轉浮力流；高樓層的風壓遠大於浮力壓差，因此腔體開口常需可調風門。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「煙囪效應浮力風量」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Heated cavity air becomes less dense and rises, creating a stack effect: the taller the cavity and the larger the temperature difference, the greater the buoyancy-driven pressure difference. A multi-storey cavity can use tens of metres of height to generate substantial natural ventilation; the west double façade of the GSW headquarters in Berlin uses its cavity as a convection shaft that supports natural ventilation of the high-rise offices. Wind pressure acts on the inlets and outlets too, reinforcing buoyancy on the windward side and cancelling or even reversing it on the leeward side; at height wind pressures far exceed stack pressures, so cavity openings usually need adjustable dampers. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Stack-driven airflow” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：浮力壓差 ΔP = ρ·g·h·ΔT/T。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Stack pressure ΔP = ρ·g·h·ΔT/T.","failure":"常見誤解：「雙層幕牆的腔體只要夠高，空氣就一定會由下往上流動。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the cavity is tall enough, air will always flow upward through it.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「煙囪效應浮力風量」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Stack-driven airflow”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-05-k1","title":"煙囪效應、風壓與腔體通風量","titleEn":"Stack effect, wind pressure and cavity airflow","text":"腔體空氣受熱後密度降低而上升，形成煙囪效應：腔體越高、溫差越大，浮力驅動的壓差就越大。多樓層式腔體可利用數十公尺的高度產生可觀的自然通風，柏林 GSW 總部的西向雙層立面即把腔體當成對流井，輔助高層辦公室的自然通風。","textEn":"Heated cavity air becomes less dense and rises, creating a stack effect: the taller the cavity and the larger the temperature difference, the greater the buoyancy-driven pressure difference. A multi-storey cavity can use tens of metres of height to generate substantial natural ventilation; the west double façade of the GSW headquarters in Berlin uses its cavity as a convection shaft that supports natural ventilation of the high-rise offices.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：雙層幕牆的腔體只要夠高，空氣就一定會由下往上流動。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the cavity is tall enough, air will always flow upward through it. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「煙囪效應、風壓與腔體通風量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Stack effect, wind pressure and cavity airflow\" is correct?","options":["雙層幕牆的腔體只要夠高，空氣就一定會由下往上流動。","外層玻璃有開口，所以幾乎不受風壓，可以用很薄的玻璃。","腔體空氣受熱後密度降低而上升，形成煙囪效應：腔體越高、溫差越大，浮力驅動的壓差就越大。"],"optionsEn":["If the cavity is tall enough, air will always flow upward through it.","Because the outer skin has openings, it sees almost no wind and can use very thin glass.","Heated cavity air becomes less dense and rises, creating a stack effect: the taller the cavity and the larger the temperature difference, the greater the buoyancy-driven pressure difference."],"answer":2,"explanation":"腔體空氣受熱後密度降低而上升，形成煙囪效應：腔體越高、溫差越大，浮力驅動的壓差就越大。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Heated cavity air becomes less dense and rises, creating a stack effect: the taller the cavity and the larger the temperature difference, the greater the buoyancy-driven pressure difference. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b089-v13-06","title":"煙囪效應、風壓與腔體通風量：定量估算","titleEn":"Stack effect, wind pressure and cavity airflow: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「煙囪效應浮力風量」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Stack-driven airflow” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：浮力壓差 ΔP = ρ·g·h·ΔT/T。h = 20 m、ΔT = 8 K、T = 300 K：ΔP = 1.2×9.81×20×8/300 ≈ 6.3 Pa。開口 Cd = 0.6、A = 0.5 m²：V = Cd·A·√(2ΔP/ρ) = 0.6×0.5×√(2×6.3/1.2) ≈ 0.97 m³/s。若迎風面 5 m/s 的風壓係數差 0.2，風壓約 0.5×1.2×5²×0.2 = 3 Pa，足以明顯改變流量。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Stack pressure ΔP = ρ·g·h·ΔT/T. With h = 20 m, ΔT = 8 K and T = 300 K: ΔP = 1.2×9.81×20×8/300 ≈ 6.3 Pa. Through an opening with Cd = 0.6 and A = 0.5 m²: V = Cd·A·√(2ΔP/ρ) = 0.6×0.5×√(2×6.3/1.2) ≈ 0.97 m³/s. A 5 m/s wind with a pressure-coefficient difference of 0.2 gives about 0.5×1.2×5²×0.2 = 3 Pa, enough to change the flow noticeably. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以風洞試驗或計算流體力學取得各風向下進出風口的風壓係數，與浮力模型合併計算全年風量分布，檢查逆流與停滯的時數；完工後以腔體內多點溫度與風速量測確認實際流向，並與控制系統紀錄的風門開度比對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Obtain pressure coefficients at inlets and outlets for each wind direction from wind-tunnel tests or CFD, combine them with the buoyancy model to compute the annual airflow distribution and count hours of reversal and stagnation; after completion confirm actual flow direction with multi-point temperature and air-speed measurement in the cavity, compared with damper positions logged by the control system.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"浮力壓差 ΔP = ρ·g·h·ΔT/T。h = 20 m、ΔT = 8 K、T = 300 K：ΔP = 1.2×9.81×20×8/300 ≈ 6.3 Pa。開口 Cd = 0.6、A = 0.5 m²：V = Cd·A·√(2ΔP/ρ) = 0.6×0.5×√(2×6.3/1.2) ≈ 0.97 m³/s。若迎風面 5 m/s 的風壓係數差 0.2，風壓約 0.5×1.2×5²×0.2 = 3 Pa，足以明顯改變流量。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Stack pressure ΔP = ρ·g·h·ΔT/T. With h = 20 m, ΔT = 8 K and T = 300 K: ΔP = 1.2×9.81×20×8/300 ≈ 6.3 Pa. Through an opening with Cd = 0.6 and A = 0.5 m²: V = Cd·A·√(2ΔP/ρ) = 0.6×0.5×√(2×6.3/1.2) ≈ 0.97 m³/s. A 5 m/s wind with a pressure-coefficient difference of 0.2 gives about 0.5×1.2×5²×0.2 = 3 Pa, enough to change the flow noticeably. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「煙囪效應、風壓與腔體通風量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Stack effect, wind pressure and cavity airflow\", which statement holds?","options":["浮力壓差 ΔP = ρ·g·h·ΔT/T。","雙層幕牆只是把一般帷幕牆多做一層，施工程序不需要改變。","腔體溫度只要量一個點就能代表整個腔體。"],"optionsEn":["Stack pressure ΔP = ρ·g·h·ΔT/T.","A double-skin façade is just an ordinary curtain wall with one more layer, so the construction process need not change.","One temperature reading represents the whole cavity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"浮力壓差 ΔP = ρ·g·h·ΔT/T。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Stack pressure ΔP = ρ·g·h·ΔT/T. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b089-v13-07","title":"煙囪效應、風壓與腔體通風量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Stack effect, wind pressure and cavity airflow: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「煙囪效應浮力風量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Stack-driven airflow” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以風洞試驗或計算流體力學取得各風向下進出風口的風壓係數，與浮力模型合併計算全年風量分布，檢查逆流與停滯的時數；完工後以腔體內多點溫度與風速量測確認實際流向，並與控制系統紀錄的風門開度比對。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Obtain pressure coefficients at inlets and outlets for each wind direction from wind-tunnel tests or CFD, combine them with the buoyancy model to compute the annual airflow distribution and count hours of reversal and stagnation; after completion confirm actual flow direction with multi-point temperature and air-speed measurement in the cavity, compared with damper positions logged by the control system. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：開口與風門的設計要同時考慮浮力、風壓與防雨，並在控制邏輯中設定強風關閉、逆流偵測與過熱開啟的條件；這些條件須由機電顧問、帷幕牆顧問與自動控制承包商共同簽認。","observationEn":"Site practice: Design openings and dampers for buoyancy, wind pressure and rain together, and set control conditions for closing in high wind, detecting reversal and opening on overheating; these conditions must be signed off jointly by the MEP consultant, façade consultant and controls contractor.","failure":"注意干擾：只以無風浮力計算開口大小，高樓層在強風時腔體出現逆流，熱空氣與汙染空氣被壓回上方樓層的開窗；或在無風炎熱的午後浮力不足，腔體停滯過熱。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Sizing openings for windless buoyancy alone lets strong wind reverse the cavity flow at upper floors, pushing hot or polluted air back into windows above; on a still, hot afternoon buoyancy may be too weak and the cavity stagnates and overheats. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以風洞試驗或計算流體力學取得各風向下進出風口的風壓係數，與浮力模型合併計算全年風量分布，檢查逆流與停滯的時數；完工後以腔體內多點溫度與風速量測確認實際流向，並與控制系統紀錄的風門開度比對。","textEn":"Obtain pressure coefficients at inlets and outlets for each wind direction from wind-tunnel tests or CFD, combine them with the buoyancy model to compute the annual airflow distribution and count hours of reversal and stagnation; after completion confirm actual flow direction with multi-point temperature and air-speed measurement in the cavity, compared with damper positions logged by the control system.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"開口與風門的設計要同時考慮浮力、風壓與防雨，並在控制邏輯中設定強風關閉、逆流偵測與過熱開啟的條件；這些條件須由機電顧問、帷幕牆顧問與自動控制承包商共同簽認。","textEn":"Design openings and dampers for buoyancy, wind pressure and rain together, and set control conditions for closing in high wind, detecting reversal and opening on overheating; these conditions must be signed off jointly by the MEP consultant, façade consultant and controls contractor.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「煙囪效應、風壓與腔體通風量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Stack effect, wind pressure and cavity airflow\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以風洞試驗或計算流體力學取得各風向下進出風口的風壓係數，與浮力模型合併計算全年風量分布，檢查逆流與停滯的時數。","腔體位於室內外之間受到保護，不需要定期清潔與檢查。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Obtain pressure coefficients at inlets and outlets for each wind direction from wind-tunnel tests or CFD, combine them with the buoyancy model to compute the annual airflow distribution and count hours of reversal and stagnation.","The cavity is sheltered between inside and outside, so it needs no regular cleaning or inspection."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以風洞試驗或計算流體力學取得各風向下進出風口的風壓係數，與浮力模型合併計算全年風量分布，檢查逆流與停滯的時數；完工後以腔體內多點溫度與風速量測確認實際流向，並與控制系統紀錄的風門開度比對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Obtain pressure coefficients at inlets and outlets for each wind direction from wind-tunnel tests or CFD, combine them with the buoyancy model to compute the annual airflow distribution and count hours of reversal and stagnation; after completion confirm actual flow direction with multi-point temperature and air-speed measurement in the cavity, compared with damper positions logged by the control system. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b089-v13-08","title":"煙囪效應、風壓與腔體通風量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Stack effect, wind pressure and cavity airflow: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「煙囪效應浮力風量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Stack-driven airflow” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只以無風浮力計算開口大小，高樓層在強風時腔體出現逆流，熱空氣與汙染空氣被壓回上方樓層的開窗；或在無風炎熱的午後浮力不足，腔體停滯過熱。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Sizing openings for windless buoyancy alone lets strong wind reverse the cavity flow at upper floors, pushing hot or polluted air back into windows above; on a still, hot afternoon buoyancy may be too weak and the cavity stagnates and overheats. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：然而外部風壓同樣作用在進出風口上，迎風面可能加強、背風面可能抵銷甚至逆轉浮力流；高樓層的風壓遠大於浮力壓差，因此腔體開口常需可調風門。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Wind pressure acts on the inlets and outlets too, reinforcing buoyancy on the windward side and cancelling or even reversing it on the leeward side; at height wind pressures far exceed stack pressures, so cavity openings usually need adjustable dampers.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「雙層幕牆的腔體只要夠高，空氣就一定會由下往上流動。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the cavity is tall enough, air will always flow upward through it.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只以無風浮力計算開口大小，高樓層在強風時腔體出現逆流，熱空氣與汙染空氣被壓回上方樓層的開窗；或在無風炎熱的午後浮力不足，腔體停滯過熱。","textEn":"Sizing openings for windless buoyancy alone lets strong wind reverse the cavity flow at upper floors, pushing hot or polluted air back into windows above; on a still, hot afternoon buoyancy may be too weak and the cavity stagnates and overheats.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「煙囪效應、風壓與腔體通風量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Stack effect, wind pressure and cavity airflow\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","外層玻璃有開口，所以幾乎不受風壓，可以用很薄的玻璃。","只以無風浮力計算開口大小，高樓層在強風時腔體出現逆流，熱空氣與汙染空氣被壓回上方樓層的開窗；或在無風炎熱的午後浮力不足，腔體停滯過熱。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Because the outer skin has openings, it sees almost no wind and can use very thin glass.","Sizing openings for windless buoyancy alone lets strong wind reverse the cavity flow at upper floors, pushing hot or polluted air back into windows above."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只以無風浮力計算開口大小，高樓層在強風時腔體出現逆流，熱空氣與汙染空氣被壓回上方樓層的開窗；或在無風炎熱的午後浮力不足，腔體停滯過熱。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Sizing openings for windless buoyancy alone lets strong wind reverse the cavity flow at upper floors, pushing hot or polluted air back into windows above; on a still, hot afternoon buoyancy may be too weak and the cavity stagnates and overheats. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b089-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「外層玻璃、托架與檢修走道結構」與「開口、風門、遮陽與樓層分隔細部」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Outer glass, brackets and maintenance-walkway structure\" and \"Openings, dampers, shading and floor-separation details\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b089-v13-09","title":"外層玻璃、托架與檢修走道結構：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Outer glass, brackets and maintenance-walkway structure: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「外層玻璃懸挑托架」如何影響雙層通風幕牆整合的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Outer-skin cantilever bracket” governs force, deformation or durability in “Double-skin ventilated facade integration”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"外層玻璃通常由樓板邊緣或內層幕牆伸出的懸挑托架支承，托架同時承托腔體內的檢修格柵走道。因此托架要承受外層玻璃自重、走道恆載與維修活載、外層玻璃承受的風壓，以及這些力在懸臂根部造成的彎矩。外層玻璃有開口時，風壓會部分進入腔體，內外兩層各自分擔的壓差隨開口比例與陣風而改變，保守做法是外層以全部外部風壓設計、內層再以腔體與室內的壓差檢核。托架穿越內層的位置也是熱橋與漏水的弱點。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「外層玻璃懸挑托架」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The outer glass is usually carried on cantilever brackets from the slab edge or the inner curtain wall, and the same brackets support the grating walkway in the cavity. The brackets must therefore carry outer-glass self-weight, walkway dead and maintenance live loads, wind on the outer glass and the resulting moments at the cantilever root. Where the outer skin has openings, wind pressure partly enters the cavity and the share taken by each skin varies with opening ratio and gusts; a conservative approach designs the outer skin for the full external pressure and checks the inner skin for the cavity-to-room difference. Where brackets pass through the inner skin they are weak points for thermal bridging and leaks. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Outer-skin cantilever bracket” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：托架間距 1.5 m、層高 3.6 m、腔深 0.9 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With brackets at 1.5 m, 3.6 m storeys and a 0.9 m cavity: 12 mm outer glass at about 30 kg/m² gives 1.5×3.6×30×9.81 ≈ 1.59 kN, a moment of about 1.43 kN·m at 0.9 m; walkway dead load 0.5 kPa and maintenance live load 1.5 kPa on 1.5×0.9 m² give 0.675 + 2.025 = 2.70 kN, about 1.22 kN·m at 0.45 m; the bracket root sees about 2.65 kN·m in total, plus a 10.8 kN horizontal force from 2.0 kPa wind.","failure":"常見誤解：「外層玻璃有開口，所以幾乎不受風壓，可以用很薄的玻璃。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Because the outer skin has openings, it sees almost no wind and can use very thin glass.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「外層玻璃懸挑托架」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Outer-skin cantilever bracket”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-09-k1","title":"外層玻璃、托架與檢修走道結構","titleEn":"Outer glass, brackets and maintenance-walkway structure","text":"外層玻璃通常由樓板邊緣或內層幕牆伸出的懸挑托架支承，托架同時承托腔體內的檢修格柵走道。因此托架要承受外層玻璃自重、走道恆載與維修活載、外層玻璃承受的風壓，以及這些力在懸臂根部造成的彎矩。","textEn":"The outer glass is usually carried on cantilever brackets from the slab edge or the inner curtain wall, and the same brackets support the grating walkway in the cavity. The brackets must therefore carry outer-glass self-weight, walkway dead and maintenance live loads, wind on the outer glass and the resulting moments at the cantilever root.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：外層玻璃有開口，所以幾乎不受風壓，可以用很薄的玻璃。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Because the outer skin has openings, it sees almost no wind and can use very thin glass. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「外層玻璃、托架與檢修走道結構」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Outer glass, brackets and maintenance-walkway structure\" is correct?","options":["外層玻璃通常由樓板邊緣或內層幕牆伸出的懸挑托架支承，托架同時承托腔體內的檢修格柵走道。","外層玻璃有開口，所以幾乎不受風壓，可以用很薄的玻璃。","腔體開口只要外觀上夠大，通風量就足夠。"],"optionsEn":["The outer glass is usually carried on cantilever brackets from the slab edge or the inner curtain wall, and the same brackets support the grating walkway in the cavity.","Because the outer skin has openings, it sees almost no wind and can use very thin glass.","If cavity openings look large enough, the airflow will be sufficient."],"answer":0,"explanation":"外層玻璃通常由樓板邊緣或內層幕牆伸出的懸挑托架支承，托架同時承托腔體內的檢修格柵走道。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The outer glass is usually carried on cantilever brackets from the slab edge or the inner curtain wall, and the same brackets support the grating walkway in the cavity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b089-v13-10","title":"外層玻璃、托架與檢修走道結構：定量估算","titleEn":"Outer glass, brackets and maintenance-walkway structure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「外層玻璃懸挑托架」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Outer-skin cantilever bracket” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：托架間距 1.5 m、層高 3.6 m、腔深 0.9 m。外層 12 mm 玻璃約 30 kg/m²：1.5×3.6×30×9.81 ≈ 1.59 kN，力臂 0.9 m 彎矩 ≈ 1.43 kN·m；走道恆載 0.5 kPa 與維修活載 1.5 kPa 作用於 1.5×0.9 m²，合力 0.675 + 2.025 = 2.70 kN，力臂 0.45 m 彎矩 ≈ 1.22 kN·m；托架根部合計約 2.65 kN·m，另有 2.0 kPa 風壓造成的 10.8 kN 水平力。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With brackets at 1.5 m, 3.6 m storeys and a 0.9 m cavity: 12 mm outer glass at about 30 kg/m² gives 1.5×3.6×30×9.81 ≈ 1.59 kN, a moment of about 1.43 kN·m at 0.9 m; walkway dead load 0.5 kPa and maintenance live load 1.5 kPa on 1.5×0.9 m² give 0.675 + 2.025 = 2.70 kN, about 1.22 kN·m at 0.45 m; the bracket root sees about 2.65 kN·m in total, plus a 10.8 kN horizontal force from 2.0 kPa wind. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：托架與走道的結構計算須涵蓋恆載、維修活載、風壓與可能的人員墜落荷重組合，並確認根部連接、樓板邊緣錨栓與內層幕牆框料的承載；以樣品牆或原型托架做載重試驗，量測撓度與殘餘變形，並檢查走道格柵的防墜與防滑。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Bracket and walkway calculations must cover combinations of dead load, maintenance live load, wind and any fall-arrest loads, and confirm the capacity of the root connection, slab-edge anchors and inner curtain-wall frames; load-test a mock-up or prototype bracket for deflection and residual set, and check the grating for fall protection and slip resistance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"托架間距 1.5 m、層高 3.6 m、腔深 0.9 m。外層 12 mm 玻璃約 30 kg/m²：1.5×3.6×30×9.81 ≈ 1.59 kN，力臂 0.9 m 彎矩 ≈ 1.43 kN·m；走道恆載 0.5 kPa 與維修活載 1.5 kPa 作用於 1.5×0.9 m²，合力 0.675 + 2.025 = 2.70 kN，力臂 0.45 m 彎矩 ≈ 1.22 kN·m；托架根部合計約 2.65 kN·m，另有 2.0 kPa 風壓造成的 10.8 kN 水平力。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"With brackets at 1.5 m, 3.6 m storeys and a 0.9 m cavity: 12 mm outer glass at about 30 kg/m² gives 1.5×3.6×30×9.81 ≈ 1.59 kN, a moment of about 1.43 kN·m at 0.9 m; walkway dead load 0.5 kPa and maintenance live load 1.5 kPa on 1.5×0.9 m² give 0.675 + 2.025 = 2.70 kN, about 1.22 kN·m at 0.45 m; the bracket root sees about 2.65 kN·m in total, plus a 10.8 kN horizontal force from 2.0 kPa wind. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「外層玻璃、托架與檢修走道結構」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Outer glass, brackets and maintenance-walkway structure\", which statement holds?","options":["雙層幕牆是被動式設計，完工後不需要控制系統試運轉。","托架間距 1.5 m、層高 3.6 m、腔深 0.9 m。","雙層幕牆的外層玻璃可以擋住火焰，所以腔體不需要防火設計。"],"optionsEn":["A double-skin façade is passive, so it needs no control commissioning after completion.","With brackets at 1.5 m, 3.6 m storeys and a 0.9 m cavity: 12 mm outer glass at about 30 kg/m² gives 1.5×3.6×30×9.81 ≈ 1.59 kN, a moment of about 1.43 kN·m at 0.9 m.","The outer glass of a double skin stops flames, so the cavity needs no fire design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"托架間距 1.5 m、層高 3.6 m、腔深 0.9 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With brackets at 1.5 m, 3.6 m storeys and a 0.9 m cavity: 12 mm outer glass at about 30 kg/m² gives 1.5×3.6×30×9.81 ≈ 1.59 kN, a moment of about 1.43 kN·m at 0.9 m; walkway dead load 0.5 kPa and maintenance live load 1.5 kPa on 1.5×0.9 m² give 0.675 + 2.025 = 2.70 kN, about 1.22 kN·m at 0.45 m; the bracket root sees about 2.65 kN·m in total, plus a 10.8 kN horizontal force from 2.0 kPa wind. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b089-v13-11","title":"外層玻璃、托架與檢修走道結構：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Outer glass, brackets and maintenance-walkway structure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「外層玻璃懸挑托架」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Outer-skin cantilever bracket” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"托架與走道的結構計算須涵蓋恆載、維修活載、風壓與可能的人員墜落荷重組合，並確認根部連接、樓板邊緣錨栓與內層幕牆框料的承載；以樣品牆或原型托架做載重試驗，量測撓度與殘餘變形，並檢查走道格柵的防墜與防滑。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Bracket and walkway calculations must cover combinations of dead load, maintenance live load, wind and any fall-arrest loads, and confirm the capacity of the root connection, slab-edge anchors and inner curtain-wall frames; load-test a mock-up or prototype bracket for deflection and residual set, and check the grating for fall protection and slip resistance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：外層玻璃採膠合玻璃以防破裂墜落，托架與走道的設計荷重、防墜錨點與允許人數須標示在現場與維護手冊；托架穿越內層處的斷熱與防水細部須在樣品牆中驗證，經帷幕牆顧問核可後才可量產。","observationEn":"Site practice: Use laminated outer glass so broken glass does not fall, and post the design loads, fall-arrest anchors and permitted number of people for brackets and walkways on site and in the maintenance manual; thermal-break and waterproofing details where brackets cross the inner skin must be proven on the mock-up and approved by the façade consultant before production.","failure":"注意干擾：托架只以玻璃自重設計而忽略檢修人員與工具荷重，維修時托架下垂、外層玻璃受扭而破裂；托架以鋼件直接穿過內層鋁框且未斷熱，冬季穿越點結露並生鏽漏水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Brackets designed only for glass weight, ignoring maintenance staff and tools, sag during cleaning and twist the outer glass until it breaks; steel brackets passing straight through aluminium inner frames without a thermal break condense at each penetration in winter, then rust and leak. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"托架與走道的結構計算須涵蓋恆載、維修活載、風壓與可能的人員墜落荷重組合，並確認根部連接、樓板邊緣錨栓與內層幕牆框料的承載；以樣品牆或原型托架做載重試驗，量測撓度與殘餘變形，並檢查走道格柵的防墜與防滑。","textEn":"Bracket and walkway calculations must cover combinations of dead load, maintenance live load, wind and any fall-arrest loads, and confirm the capacity of the root connection, slab-edge anchors and inner curtain-wall frames; load-test a mock-up or prototype bracket for deflection and residual set, and check the grating for fall protection and slip resistance.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"外層玻璃採膠合玻璃以防破裂墜落，托架與走道的設計荷重、防墜錨點與允許人數須標示在現場與維護手冊；托架穿越內層處的斷熱與防水細部須在樣品牆中驗證，經帷幕牆顧問核可後才可量產。","textEn":"Use laminated outer glass so broken glass does not fall, and post the design loads, fall-arrest anchors and permitted number of people for brackets and walkways on site and in the maintenance manual; thermal-break and waterproofing details where brackets cross the inner skin must be proven on the mock-up and approved by the façade consultant before production.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「外層玻璃、托架與檢修走道結構」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Outer glass, brackets and maintenance-walkway structure\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","雙層幕牆的節能效果在設計模擬時就已確定，完工後不需要驗證。","托架與走道的結構計算須涵蓋恆載、維修活載、風壓與可能的人員墜落荷重組合，並確認根部連接、樓板邊緣錨栓與內層幕牆框料的承載。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The energy savings of a double skin are fixed by the design simulation and need no verification after completion.","Bracket and walkway calculations must cover combinations of dead load, maintenance live load, wind and any fall-arrest loads, and confirm the capacity of the root connection, slab-edge anchors and inner curtain-wall frames."],"answer":2,"explanation":"托架與走道的結構計算須涵蓋恆載、維修活載、風壓與可能的人員墜落荷重組合，並確認根部連接、樓板邊緣錨栓與內層幕牆框料的承載；以樣品牆或原型托架做載重試驗，量測撓度與殘餘變形，並檢查走道格柵的防墜與防滑。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Bracket and walkway calculations must cover combinations of dead load, maintenance live load, wind and any fall-arrest loads, and confirm the capacity of the root connection, slab-edge anchors and inner curtain-wall frames; load-test a mock-up or prototype bracket for deflection and residual set, and check the grating for fall protection and slip resistance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b089-v13-12","title":"外層玻璃、托架與檢修走道結構：失效診斷","titleEn":"Outer glass, brackets and maintenance-walkway structure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「外層玻璃懸挑托架」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Outer-skin cantilever bracket” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"托架只以玻璃自重設計而忽略檢修人員與工具荷重，維修時托架下垂、外層玻璃受扭而破裂；托架以鋼件直接穿過內層鋁框且未斷熱，冬季穿越點結露並生鏽漏水。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Brackets designed only for glass weight, ignoring maintenance staff and tools, sag during cleaning and twist the outer glass until it breaks; steel brackets passing straight through aluminium inner frames without a thermal break condense at each penetration in winter, then rust and leak. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：托架穿越內層的位置也是熱橋與漏水的弱點。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Where brackets pass through the inner skin they are weak points for thermal bridging and leaks.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「外層玻璃有開口，所以幾乎不受風壓，可以用很薄的玻璃。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Because the outer skin has openings, it sees almost no wind and can use very thin glass.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"托架只以玻璃自重設計而忽略檢修人員與工具荷重，維修時托架下垂、外層玻璃受扭而破裂；托架以鋼件直接穿過內層鋁框且未斷熱，冬季穿越點結露並生鏽漏水。","textEn":"Brackets designed only for glass weight, ignoring maintenance staff and tools, sag during cleaning and twist the outer glass until it breaks; steel brackets passing straight through aluminium inner frames without a thermal break condense at each penetration in winter, then rust and leak.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「外層玻璃、托架與檢修走道結構」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Outer glass, brackets and maintenance-walkway structure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["托架只以玻璃自重設計而忽略檢修人員與工具荷重，維修時托架下垂、外層玻璃受扭而破裂；托架以鋼件直接穿過內層鋁框且未斷熱，冬季穿越點結露並生鏽漏水。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","腔體開口只要外觀上夠大，通風量就足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Brackets designed only for glass weight, ignoring maintenance staff and tools, sag during cleaning and twist the outer glass until it breaks.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","If cavity openings look large enough, the airflow will be sufficient."],"answer":0,"explanation":"托架只以玻璃自重設計而忽略檢修人員與工具荷重，維修時托架下垂、外層玻璃受扭而破裂；托架以鋼件直接穿過內層鋁框且未斷熱，冬季穿越點結露並生鏽漏水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Brackets designed only for glass weight, ignoring maintenance staff and tools, sag during cleaning and twist the outer glass until it breaks; steel brackets passing straight through aluminium inner frames without a thermal break condense at each penetration in winter, then rust and leak. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b089-v13-13","title":"開口、風門、遮陽與樓層分隔細部：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Openings, dampers, shading and floor-separation details: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「進出風口與防蟲網」如何影響雙層通風幕牆整合的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Inlet, outlet and insect screens” governs force, deformation or durability in “Double-skin ventilated facade integration”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"腔體的性能最終由細部決定：進出風口的有效面積、百葉格柵與防蟲網造成的阻力、風門的密合度、遮陽百葉與玻璃之間的距離，以及每層或每數層的水平分隔。走廊式與箱窗式腔體在每層設水平分隔，可阻斷聲音、氣味與煙在樓層間傳遞，但限制了浮力高度；多樓層式腔體通風較強，卻必須以其他方式處理防火與隔音。倫敦聖瑪莉斧街 30 號的螺旋採光井每六層設防火隔斷，就是在通風效益與防火之間折衷的例子。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「進出風口與防蟲網」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cavity performance is ultimately decided by details: the effective area of inlets and outlets, the resistance of louvres and insect screens, the tightness of dampers, the spacing between blinds and glass, and horizontal divisions at every floor or every few floors. Corridor and box-window cavities divided at each floor stop sound, odours and smoke passing between floors but limit the buoyancy height; multi-storey cavities ventilate better but must deal with fire and acoustics in other ways. The spiralling light wells of 30 St Mary Axe in London, interrupted by fire breaks every sixth floor, are an example of compromise between ventilation benefit and fire safety. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Inlet, outlet and insect screens” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：所需有效開口 Cd·A = 0.3 m²，百葉格柵自由面積比 50%、流量係數 0.6：毛面積 = 0.3/(0.6×0.5) = 1.0 m²，在 3.0 m 寬的開間即需高約 0.33 m 的開口帶；加裝使自由面積再降至 60% 的防蟲網，毛面積增為 0.3/(0.6×0.5×0.6) ≈ 1.67 m²，約高 0.56 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For a required effective opening Cd·A = 0.3 m² with a louvre free-area ratio of 50% and a discharge coefficient of 0.6, the gross area is 0.3/(0.6×0.5) = 1.0 m², an opening band about 0.33 m high across a 3.0 m bay; adding an insect screen that cuts free area to 60% raises the gross area to 0.3/(0.6×0.5×0.6) ≈ 1.67 m², about 0.56 m high.","failure":"常見誤解：「腔體開口只要外觀上夠大，通風量就足夠。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If cavity openings look large enough, the airflow will be sufficient.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「進出風口與防蟲網」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Inlet, outlet and insect screens”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-13-k1","title":"開口、風門、遮陽與樓層分隔細部","titleEn":"Openings, dampers, shading and floor-separation details","text":"腔體的性能最終由細部決定：進出風口的有效面積、百葉格柵與防蟲網造成的阻力、風門的密合度、遮陽百葉與玻璃之間的距離，以及每層或每數層的水平分隔。走廊式與箱窗式腔體在每層設水平分隔，可阻斷聲音、氣味與煙在樓層間傳遞，但限制了浮力高度；多樓層式腔體通風較強，卻必須以其他方式處理防火與隔音。","textEn":"Cavity performance is ultimately decided by details: the effective area of inlets and outlets, the resistance of louvres and insect screens, the tightness of dampers, the spacing between blinds and glass, and horizontal divisions at every floor or every few floors. Corridor and box-window cavities divided at each floor stop sound, odours and smoke passing between floors but limit the buoyancy height; multi-storey cavities ventilate better but must deal with fire and acoustics in other ways.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：腔體開口只要外觀上夠大，通風量就足夠。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If cavity openings look large enough, the airflow will be sufficient. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「開口、風門、遮陽與樓層分隔細部」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Openings, dampers, shading and floor-separation details\" is correct?","options":["腔體開口只要外觀上夠大，通風量就足夠。","腔體的性能最終由細部決定：進出風口的有效面積、百葉格柵與防蟲網造成的阻力、風門的密合度、遮陽百葉與玻璃之間的距離，以及每層或每數層的水平分隔。","雙層幕牆只是把一般帷幕牆多做一層，施工程序不需要改變。"],"optionsEn":["If cavity openings look large enough, the airflow will be sufficient.","Cavity performance is ultimately decided by details: the effective area of inlets and outlets, the resistance of louvres and insect screens, the tightness of dampers, the spacing between blinds and glass, and horizontal divisions at every floor or every few floors.","A double-skin façade is just an ordinary curtain wall with one more layer, so the construction process need not change."],"answer":1,"explanation":"腔體的性能最終由細部決定：進出風口的有效面積、百葉格柵與防蟲網造成的阻力、風門的密合度、遮陽百葉與玻璃之間的距離，以及每層或每數層的水平分隔。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cavity performance is ultimately decided by details: the effective area of inlets and outlets, the resistance of louvres and insect screens, the tightness of dampers, the spacing between blinds and glass, and horizontal divisions at every floor or every few floors. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b089-v13-14","title":"開口、風門、遮陽與樓層分隔細部：定量估算","titleEn":"Openings, dampers, shading and floor-separation details: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「進出風口與防蟲網」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Inlet, outlet and insect screens” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：所需有效開口 Cd·A = 0.3 m²，百葉格柵自由面積比 50%、流量係數 0.6：毛面積 = 0.3/(0.6×0.5) = 1.0 m²，在 3.0 m 寬的開間即需高約 0.33 m 的開口帶；加裝使自由面積再降至 60% 的防蟲網，毛面積增為 0.3/(0.6×0.5×0.6) ≈ 1.67 m²，約高 0.56 m。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For a required effective opening Cd·A = 0.3 m² with a louvre free-area ratio of 50% and a discharge coefficient of 0.6, the gross area is 0.3/(0.6×0.5) = 1.0 m², an opening band about 0.33 m high across a 3.0 m bay; adding an insect screen that cuts free area to 60% raises the gross area to 0.3/(0.6×0.5×0.6) ≈ 1.67 m², about 0.56 m high. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以廠商試驗的百葉與防蟲網壓損資料計算實際有效面積，並在樣品牆中量測開口處風速；水平分隔須確認材料耐火時效、與內外兩層的接合密封，以及檢修人員通過時的開閉方式；遮陽百葉與玻璃的距離須檢查熱應力與百葉擺動碰撞。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Calculate actual effective area from the manufacturer's tested pressure-loss data for louvres and insect screens, and measure air speed at openings on the mock-up; for horizontal divisions confirm fire rating, seals to both skins and how they open for maintenance staff to pass; check blind-to-glass spacing for thermal stress and blind swing contact.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"所需有效開口 Cd·A = 0.3 m²，百葉格柵自由面積比 50%、流量係數 0.6：毛面積 = 0.3/(0.6×0.5) = 1.0 m²，在 3.0 m 寬的開間即需高約 0.33 m 的開口帶；加裝使自由面積再降至 60% 的防蟲網，毛面積增為 0.3/(0.6×0.5×0.6) ≈ 1.67 m²，約高 0.56 m。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"For a required effective opening Cd·A = 0.3 m² with a louvre free-area ratio of 50% and a discharge coefficient of 0.6, the gross area is 0.3/(0.6×0.5) = 1.0 m², an opening band about 0.33 m high across a 3.0 m bay; adding an insect screen that cuts free area to 60% raises the gross area to 0.3/(0.6×0.5×0.6) ≈ 1.67 m², about 0.56 m high. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「開口、風門、遮陽與樓層分隔細部」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Openings, dampers, shading and floor-separation details\", which statement holds?","options":["腔體溫度只要量一個點就能代表整個腔體。","腔體位於室內外之間受到保護，不需要定期清潔與檢查。","所需有效開口 Cd·A = 0.3 m²，百葉格柵自由面積比 50%、流量係數 0.6：毛面積 = 0.3/(0.6×0.5) = 1.0 m²，在 3.0 m 寬的開間即需高約 0.33 m 的開口帶。"],"optionsEn":["One temperature reading represents the whole cavity.","The cavity is sheltered between inside and outside, so it needs no regular cleaning or inspection.","For a required effective opening Cd·A = 0.3 m² with a louvre free-area ratio of 50% and a discharge coefficient of 0.6, the gross area is 0.3/(0.6×0.5) = 1.0 m², an opening band about 0.33 m high across a 3.0 m bay."],"answer":2,"explanation":"所需有效開口 Cd·A = 0.3 m²，百葉格柵自由面積比 50%、流量係數 0.6：毛面積 = 0.3/(0.6×0.5) = 1.0 m²，在 3.0 m 寬的開間即需高約 0.33 m 的開口帶；加裝使自由面積再降至 60% 的防蟲網，毛面積增為 0.3/(0.6×0.5×0.6) ≈ 1.67 m²，約高 0.56 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For a required effective opening Cd·A = 0.3 m² with a louvre free-area ratio of 50% and a discharge coefficient of 0.6, the gross area is 0.3/(0.6×0.5) = 1.0 m², an opening band about 0.33 m high across a 3.0 m bay; adding an insect screen that cuts free area to 60% raises the gross area to 0.3/(0.6×0.5×0.6) ≈ 1.67 m², about 0.56 m high. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b089-v13-15","title":"開口、風門、遮陽與樓層分隔細部：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Openings, dampers, shading and floor-separation details: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「進出風口與防蟲網」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Inlet, outlet and insect screens” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以廠商試驗的百葉與防蟲網壓損資料計算實際有效面積，並在樣品牆中量測開口處風速；水平分隔須確認材料耐火時效、與內外兩層的接合密封，以及檢修人員通過時的開閉方式；遮陽百葉與玻璃的距離須檢查熱應力與百葉擺動碰撞。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Calculate actual effective area from the manufacturer's tested pressure-loss data for louvres and insect screens, and measure air speed at openings on the mock-up; for horizontal divisions confirm fire rating, seals to both skins and how they open for maintenance staff to pass; check blind-to-glass spacing for thermal stress and blind swing contact. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：開口與防蟲網要設計成可從腔體內安全拆卸清潔，並在維護手冊列出清潔週期與壓損檢查方法；樓層水平分隔的位置與耐火時效須由防火工程師與帷幕牆顧問共同確認，並經主管機關審查。","observationEn":"Site practice: Design openings and insect screens to be removed and cleaned safely from inside the cavity, and list the cleaning interval and pressure-loss check in the maintenance manual; positions and fire ratings of horizontal divisions must be agreed by the fire engineer and façade consultant and reviewed by the authority.","failure":"注意干擾：設計時以開口毛面積計算風量，加上百葉與防蟲網後實際有效面積只剩三成，腔體長期過熱；防蟲網積塵或被鳥巢堵塞後風量再降，而沒有人知道要清理。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Calculating airflow from gross opening area means that louvres and insect screens leave only about a third of the effective area and the cavity overheats chronically; once screens clog with dust or bird nests, airflow falls further and nobody knows they need cleaning. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以廠商試驗的百葉與防蟲網壓損資料計算實際有效面積，並在樣品牆中量測開口處風速；水平分隔須確認材料耐火時效、與內外兩層的接合密封，以及檢修人員通過時的開閉方式；遮陽百葉與玻璃的距離須檢查熱應力與百葉擺動碰撞。","textEn":"Calculate actual effective area from the manufacturer's tested pressure-loss data for louvres and insect screens, and measure air speed at openings on the mock-up; for horizontal divisions confirm fire rating, seals to both skins and how they open for maintenance staff to pass; check blind-to-glass spacing for thermal stress and blind swing contact.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"開口與防蟲網要設計成可從腔體內安全拆卸清潔，並在維護手冊列出清潔週期與壓損檢查方法；樓層水平分隔的位置與耐火時效須由防火工程師與帷幕牆顧問共同確認，並經主管機關審查。","textEn":"Design openings and insect screens to be removed and cleaned safely from inside the cavity, and list the cleaning interval and pressure-loss check in the maintenance manual; positions and fire ratings of horizontal divisions must be agreed by the fire engineer and façade consultant and reviewed by the authority.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「開口、風門、遮陽與樓層分隔細部」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Openings, dampers, shading and floor-separation details\"?","options":["以廠商試驗的百葉與防蟲網壓損資料計算實際有效面積，並在樣品牆中量測開口處風速。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","多加一層玻璃一定能減少建築的空調耗能。"],"optionsEn":["Calculate actual effective area from the manufacturer's tested pressure-loss data for louvres and insect screens, and measure air speed at openings on the mock-up.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Adding a second layer of glass always reduces air-conditioning energy."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以廠商試驗的百葉與防蟲網壓損資料計算實際有效面積，並在樣品牆中量測開口處風速；水平分隔須確認材料耐火時效、與內外兩層的接合密封，以及檢修人員通過時的開閉方式；遮陽百葉與玻璃的距離須檢查熱應力與百葉擺動碰撞。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Calculate actual effective area from the manufacturer's tested pressure-loss data for louvres and insect screens, and measure air speed at openings on the mock-up; for horizontal divisions confirm fire rating, seals to both skins and how they open for maintenance staff to pass; check blind-to-glass spacing for thermal stress and blind swing contact. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b089-v13-16","title":"開口、風門、遮陽與樓層分隔細部：失效診斷","titleEn":"Openings, dampers, shading and floor-separation details: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「進出風口與防蟲網」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Inlet, outlet and insect screens” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"設計時以開口毛面積計算風量，加上百葉與防蟲網後實際有效面積只剩三成，腔體長期過熱；防蟲網積塵或被鳥巢堵塞後風量再降，而沒有人知道要清理。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Calculating airflow from gross opening area means that louvres and insect screens leave only about a third of the effective area and the cavity overheats chronically; once screens clog with dust or bird nests, airflow falls further and nobody knows they need cleaning. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：倫敦聖瑪莉斧街 30 號的螺旋採光井每六層設防火隔斷，就是在通風效益與防火之間折衷的例子。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The spiralling light wells of 30 St Mary Axe in London, interrupted by fire breaks every sixth floor, are an example of compromise between ventilation benefit and fire safety.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「腔體開口只要外觀上夠大，通風量就足夠。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If cavity openings look large enough, the airflow will be sufficient.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"設計時以開口毛面積計算風量，加上百葉與防蟲網後實際有效面積只剩三成，腔體長期過熱；防蟲網積塵或被鳥巢堵塞後風量再降，而沒有人知道要清理。","textEn":"Calculating airflow from gross opening area means that louvres and insect screens leave only about a third of the effective area and the cavity overheats chronically; once screens clog with dust or bird nests, airflow falls further and nobody knows they need cleaning.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「開口、風門、遮陽與樓層分隔細部」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Openings, dampers, shading and floor-separation details\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","設計時以開口毛面積計算風量，加上百葉與防蟲網後實際有效面積只剩三成，腔體長期過熱；防蟲網積塵或被鳥巢堵塞後風量再降，而沒有人知道要清理。","雙層幕牆只是把一般帷幕牆多做一層，施工程序不需要改變。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Calculating airflow from gross opening area means that louvres and insect screens leave only about a third of the effective area and the cavity overheats chronically.","A double-skin façade is just an ordinary curtain wall with one more layer, so the construction process need not change."],"answer":1,"explanation":"設計時以開口毛面積計算風量，加上百葉與防蟲網後實際有效面積只剩三成，腔體長期過熱；防蟲網積塵或被鳥巢堵塞後風量再降，而沒有人知道要清理。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Calculating airflow from gross opening area means that louvres and insect screens leave only about a third of the effective area and the cavity overheats chronically; once screens clog with dust or bird nests, airflow falls further and nobody knows they need cleaning. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b089-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「雙層單元的預組、吊裝與施工整合」與「控制系統整合與試運轉」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Prefabrication, lifting and construction integration of double-skin units\" and \"Control-system integration and commissioning\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b089-v13-17","title":"雙層單元的預組、吊裝與施工整合：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Prefabrication, lifting and construction integration of double-skin units: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「預組箱窗單元」如何影響雙層通風幕牆整合的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Prefabricated box-window unit” governs force, deformation or durability in “Double-skin ventilated facade integration”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"雙層幕牆可以分別安裝內層與外層，也可以在工廠把內外兩層、腔體百葉與風門組成一個箱窗單元整體吊裝。整體單元減少現場工序與腔體汙染，但重量與尺寸明顯增加，吊裝設備、樓層運輸與錨件都要重新檢討；分開安裝則需要協調兩組工班與托架的施工順序，並在外層封閉前完成腔體內所有電線、馬達與感測器。無論哪一種，腔體一旦封閉，任何遺漏的接線或碎屑都很難處理。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「預組箱窗單元」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A double-skin façade can be installed as separate inner and outer layers, or factory-assembled with both skins, cavity blinds and dampers into box-window units lifted as one piece. Complete units reduce site operations and cavity contamination but are much heavier and larger, so lifting equipment, floor logistics and anchors must be reconsidered; separate installation requires coordinating two crews and the bracket sequence, and completing every cable, motor and sensor in the cavity before the outer skin closes. Either way, once the cavity is closed, any missed wiring or debris is hard to deal with. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Prefabricated box-window unit” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：3.0×3.6 m = 10.8 m² 單元：單層幕牆約 60 kg/m²，重約 648 kg；雙層箱窗單元（內層 50、外層玻璃 30、框架與百葉 25 kg/m²）約 105 kg/m²，重約 1,134 kg，為單層的 1.75 倍。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For a 3.0×3.6 m = 10.8 m² unit: a single skin at about 60 kg/m² weighs about 648 kg; a box-window double-skin unit (inner 50, outer glass 30, frame and blinds 25 kg/m²) at about 105 kg/m² weighs about 1,134 kg, 1.75 times as much.","failure":"常見誤解：「雙層幕牆只是把一般帷幕牆多做一層，施工程序不需要改變。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A double-skin façade is just an ordinary curtain wall with one more layer, so the construction process need not change.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「預組箱窗單元」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Prefabricated box-window unit”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-17-k1","title":"雙層單元的預組、吊裝與施工整合","titleEn":"Prefabrication, lifting and construction integration of double-skin units","text":"雙層幕牆可以分別安裝內層與外層，也可以在工廠把內外兩層、腔體百葉與風門組成一個箱窗單元整體吊裝。整體單元減少現場工序與腔體汙染，但重量與尺寸明顯增加，吊裝設備、樓層運輸與錨件都要重新檢討；分開安裝則需要協調兩組工班與托架的施工順序，並在外層封閉前完成腔體內所有電線、馬達與感測器。","textEn":"A double-skin façade can be installed as separate inner and outer layers, or factory-assembled with both skins, cavity blinds and dampers into box-window units lifted as one piece. Complete units reduce site operations and cavity contamination but are much heavier and larger, so lifting equipment, floor logistics and anchors must be reconsidered; separate installation requires coordinating two crews and the bracket sequence, and completing every cable, motor and sensor in the cavity before the outer skin closes.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：雙層幕牆只是把一般帷幕牆多做一層，施工程序不需要改變。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A double-skin façade is just an ordinary curtain wall with one more layer, so the construction process need not change. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「雙層單元的預組、吊裝與施工整合」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Prefabrication, lifting and construction integration of double-skin units\" is correct?","options":["雙層幕牆只是把一般帷幕牆多做一層，施工程序不需要改變。","雙層幕牆是被動式設計，完工後不需要控制系統試運轉。","雙層幕牆可以分別安裝內層與外層，也可以在工廠把內外兩層、腔體百葉與風門組成一個箱窗單元整體吊裝。"],"optionsEn":["A double-skin façade is just an ordinary curtain wall with one more layer, so the construction process need not change.","A double-skin façade is passive, so it needs no control commissioning after completion.","A double-skin façade can be installed as separate inner and outer layers, or factory-assembled with both skins, cavity blinds and dampers into box-window units lifted as one piece."],"answer":2,"explanation":"雙層幕牆可以分別安裝內層與外層，也可以在工廠把內外兩層、腔體百葉與風門組成一個箱窗單元整體吊裝。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A double-skin façade can be installed as separate inner and outer layers, or factory-assembled with both skins, cavity blinds and dampers into box-window units lifted as one piece. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b089-v13-18","title":"雙層單元的預組、吊裝與施工整合：定量估算","titleEn":"Prefabrication, lifting and construction integration of double-skin units: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「預組箱窗單元」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Prefabricated box-window unit” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：3.0×3.6 m = 10.8 m² 單元：單層幕牆約 60 kg/m²，重約 648 kg；雙層箱窗單元（內層 50、外層玻璃 30、框架與百葉 25 kg/m²）約 105 kg/m²，重約 1,134 kg，為單層的 1.75 倍。若塔吊在該半徑額定 1.5 t、吊具 0.2 t，餘裕約 0.17 t。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For a 3.0×3.6 m = 10.8 m² unit: a single skin at about 60 kg/m² weighs about 648 kg; a box-window double-skin unit (inner 50, outer glass 30, frame and blinds 25 kg/m²) at about 105 kg/m² weighs about 1,134 kg, 1.75 times as much. With a 1.5 t crane rating at that radius and 0.2 t of rigging, about 0.17 t of margin remains. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較整體單元與分開安裝的吊裝重量、錨件反力、樓層暫存荷重與工期；外層封閉前設腔體檢查停止點，逐格確認百葉、馬達、感測器與線路已安裝並通電測試，腔體清潔無碎屑，並拍照紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare complete-unit and separate installation for lifting weight, anchor reactions, floor storage loads and programme; set a cavity hold point before the outer skin closes, confirming bay by bay that blinds, motors, sensors and wiring are installed and power-tested and that the cavity is clean, with photographs.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"3.0×3.6 m = 10.8 m² 單元：單層幕牆約 60 kg/m²，重約 648 kg；雙層箱窗單元（內層 50、外層玻璃 30、框架與百葉 25 kg/m²）約 105 kg/m²，重約 1,134 kg，為單層的 1.75 倍。若塔吊在該半徑額定 1.5 t、吊具 0.2 t，餘裕約 0.17 t。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"For a 3.0×3.6 m = 10.8 m² unit: a single skin at about 60 kg/m² weighs about 648 kg; a box-window double-skin unit (inner 50, outer glass 30, frame and blinds 25 kg/m²) at about 105 kg/m² weighs about 1,134 kg, 1.75 times as much. With a 1.5 t crane rating at that radius and 0.2 t of rigging, about 0.17 t of margin remains. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「雙層單元的預組、吊裝與施工整合」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Prefabrication, lifting and construction integration of double-skin units\", which statement holds?","options":["3.0×3.6 m = 10.8 m² 單元：單層幕牆約 60 kg/m²，重約 648 kg。","雙層幕牆的外層玻璃可以擋住火焰，所以腔體不需要防火設計。","雙層幕牆的節能效果在設計模擬時就已確定，完工後不需要驗證。"],"optionsEn":["For a 3.0×3.6 m = 10.8 m² unit: a single skin at about 60 kg/m² weighs about 648 kg.","The outer glass of a double skin stops flames, so the cavity needs no fire design.","The energy savings of a double skin are fixed by the design simulation and need no verification after completion."],"answer":0,"explanation":"3.0×3.6 m = 10.8 m² 單元：單層幕牆約 60 kg/m²，重約 648 kg；雙層箱窗單元（內層 50、外層玻璃 30、框架與百葉 25 kg/m²）約 105 kg/m²，重約 1,134 kg，為單層的 1.75 倍。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For a 3.0×3.6 m = 10.8 m² unit: a single skin at about 60 kg/m² weighs about 648 kg; a box-window double-skin unit (inner 50, outer glass 30, frame and blinds 25 kg/m²) at about 105 kg/m² weighs about 1,134 kg, 1.75 times as much. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b089-v13-19","title":"雙層單元的預組、吊裝與施工整合：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Prefabrication, lifting and construction integration of double-skin units: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「預組箱窗單元」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Prefabricated box-window unit” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較整體單元與分開安裝的吊裝重量、錨件反力、樓層暫存荷重與工期；外層封閉前設腔體檢查停止點，逐格確認百葉、馬達、感測器與線路已安裝並通電測試，腔體清潔無碎屑，並拍照紀錄。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare complete-unit and separate installation for lifting weight, anchor reactions, floor storage loads and programme; set a cavity hold point before the outer skin closes, confirming bay by bay that blinds, motors, sensors and wiring are installed and power-tested and that the cavity is clean, with photographs. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：施工計畫要明確劃分帷幕牆、機電與自動控制承包商在腔體內的工作界面與順序，以「腔體封閉許可」作為停止點，由三方與監造共同簽認；吊裝重量增加時須重新核算塔吊、樓板與錨件。","observationEn":"Site practice: The construction plan must define the cavity work interfaces and sequence between façade, MEP and controls contractors, with a cavity-closure permit as a hold point signed by all three and the supervising engineer; heavier lifts require cranes, slabs and anchors to be re-checked.","failure":"注意干擾：外層玻璃安裝完畢後才發現某些樓層的百葉馬達線路未接，只能拆除外層玻璃重來；腔體封閉前未清除施工粉塵與碎屑，完工後百葉卡死、感測器失準，玻璃內側也留下難以清潔的汙漬。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Finding after the outer glass is installed that blind motors on some floors were never wired means removing the outer glass and starting again; failing to clear construction dust and debris before closure leaves blinds jamming, sensors drifting and stains on inner glass faces that are hard to clean. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較整體單元與分開安裝的吊裝重量、錨件反力、樓層暫存荷重與工期；外層封閉前設腔體檢查停止點，逐格確認百葉、馬達、感測器與線路已安裝並通電測試，腔體清潔無碎屑，並拍照紀錄。","textEn":"Compare complete-unit and separate installation for lifting weight, anchor reactions, floor storage loads and programme; set a cavity hold point before the outer skin closes, confirming bay by bay that blinds, motors, sensors and wiring are installed and power-tested and that the cavity is clean, with photographs.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"施工計畫要明確劃分帷幕牆、機電與自動控制承包商在腔體內的工作界面與順序，以「腔體封閉許可」作為停止點，由三方與監造共同簽認；吊裝重量增加時須重新核算塔吊、樓板與錨件。","textEn":"The construction plan must define the cavity work interfaces and sequence between façade, MEP and controls contractors, with a cavity-closure permit as a hold point signed by all three and the supervising engineer; heavier lifts require cranes, slabs and anchors to be re-checked.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「雙層單元的預組、吊裝與施工整合」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Prefabrication, lifting and construction integration of double-skin units\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","比較整體單元與分開安裝的吊裝重量、錨件反力、樓層暫存荷重與工期。","雙層幕牆的腔體只要夠高，空氣就一定會由下往上流動。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Compare complete-unit and separate installation for lifting weight, anchor reactions, floor storage loads and programme.","If the cavity is tall enough, air will always flow upward through it."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較整體單元與分開安裝的吊裝重量、錨件反力、樓層暫存荷重與工期；外層封閉前設腔體檢查停止點，逐格確認百葉、馬達、感測器與線路已安裝並通電測試，腔體清潔無碎屑，並拍照紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare complete-unit and separate installation for lifting weight, anchor reactions, floor storage loads and programme; set a cavity hold point before the outer skin closes, confirming bay by bay that blinds, motors, sensors and wiring are installed and power-tested and that the cavity is clean, with photographs. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b089-v13-20","title":"雙層單元的預組、吊裝與施工整合：失效診斷","titleEn":"Prefabrication, lifting and construction integration of double-skin units: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「預組箱窗單元」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Prefabricated box-window unit” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"外層玻璃安裝完畢後才發現某些樓層的百葉馬達線路未接，只能拆除外層玻璃重來；腔體封閉前未清除施工粉塵與碎屑，完工後百葉卡死、感測器失準，玻璃內側也留下難以清潔的汙漬。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Finding after the outer glass is installed that blind motors on some floors were never wired means removing the outer glass and starting again; failing to clear construction dust and debris before closure leaves blinds jamming, sensors drifting and stains on inner glass faces that are hard to clean. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：無論哪一種，腔體一旦封閉，任何遺漏的接線或碎屑都很難處理。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Either way, once the cavity is closed, any missed wiring or debris is hard to deal with.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「雙層幕牆只是把一般帷幕牆多做一層，施工程序不需要改變。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A double-skin façade is just an ordinary curtain wall with one more layer, so the construction process need not change.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"外層玻璃安裝完畢後才發現某些樓層的百葉馬達線路未接，只能拆除外層玻璃重來；腔體封閉前未清除施工粉塵與碎屑，完工後百葉卡死、感測器失準，玻璃內側也留下難以清潔的汙漬。","textEn":"Finding after the outer glass is installed that blind motors on some floors were never wired means removing the outer glass and starting again; failing to clear construction dust and debris before closure leaves blinds jamming, sensors drifting and stains on inner glass faces that are hard to clean.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「雙層單元的預組、吊裝與施工整合」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Prefabrication, lifting and construction integration of double-skin units\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","雙層幕牆是被動式設計，完工後不需要控制系統試運轉。","外層玻璃安裝完畢後才發現某些樓層的百葉馬達線路未接，只能拆除外層玻璃重來。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A double-skin façade is passive, so it needs no control commissioning after completion.","Finding after the outer glass is installed that blind motors on some floors were never wired means removing the outer glass and starting again."],"answer":2,"explanation":"外層玻璃安裝完畢後才發現某些樓層的百葉馬達線路未接，只能拆除外層玻璃重來；腔體封閉前未清除施工粉塵與碎屑，完工後百葉卡死、感測器失準，玻璃內側也留下難以清潔的汙漬。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Finding after the outer glass is installed that blind motors on some floors were never wired means removing the outer glass and starting again; failing to clear construction dust and debris before closure leaves blinds jamming, sensors drifting and stains on inner glass faces that are hard to clean. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b089-v13-21","title":"控制系統整合與試運轉：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Control-system integration and commissioning: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「風門百葉控制點」如何影響雙層通風幕牆整合的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Damper and blind control points” governs force, deformation or durability in “Double-skin ventilated facade integration”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"雙層幕牆是一個需要「操作」的立面：風門開度、百葉角度、內層窗戶與空調系統必須依日射、室外溫度、風速、雨量與腔體溫度協同動作。曼尼托巴水電大樓的東西向雙層立面內外兩層都設可開啟窗，配合中庭與太陽能煙囪通風，就仰賴建築自動化系統整合。控制邏輯若只在設計說明中描述而未經實際試運轉，常出現感測器位置不當、指令衝突或手動覆寫後無法回復等問題，使立面長期停在不利的狀態。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「風門百葉控制點」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A double-skin façade has to be operated: damper positions, blind angles, inner windows and HVAC must act together according to irradiance, outdoor temperature, wind speed, rain and cavity temperature. Manitoba Hydro Place, with operable windows in both layers of its east and west double façades working with atria and a solar chimney, relies on building-automation integration in exactly this way. Control logic described in a design report but never commissioned often suffers from poorly sited sensors, conflicting commands or manual overrides that never reset, leaving the façade stuck in an unfavourable state for years. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Damper and blind control points” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：60 層、每層 40 個開間，每開間 2 個風門與 1 個百葉馬達：致動器 60×40×3 = 7,200 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With 60 floors, 40 bays per floor and 2 dampers plus 1 blind motor per bay, there are 60×40×3 = 7,200 actuators.","failure":"常見誤解：「雙層幕牆是被動式設計，完工後不需要控制系統試運轉。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A double-skin façade is passive, so it needs no control commissioning after completion.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「風門百葉控制點」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Damper and blind control points”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-21-k1","title":"控制系統整合與試運轉","titleEn":"Control-system integration and commissioning","text":"雙層幕牆是一個需要「操作」的立面：風門開度、百葉角度、內層窗戶與空調系統必須依日射、室外溫度、風速、雨量與腔體溫度協同動作。曼尼托巴水電大樓的東西向雙層立面內外兩層都設可開啟窗，配合中庭與太陽能煙囪通風，就仰賴建築自動化系統整合。","textEn":"A double-skin façade has to be operated: damper positions, blind angles, inner windows and HVAC must act together according to irradiance, outdoor temperature, wind speed, rain and cavity temperature. Manitoba Hydro Place, with operable windows in both layers of its east and west double façades working with atria and a solar chimney, relies on building-automation integration in exactly this way.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：雙層幕牆是被動式設計，完工後不需要控制系統試運轉。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A double-skin façade is passive, so it needs no control commissioning after completion. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制系統整合與試運轉」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control-system integration and commissioning\" is correct?","options":["雙層幕牆是一個需要「操作」的立面：風門開度、百葉角度、內層窗戶與空調系統必須依日射、室外溫度、風速、雨量與腔體溫度協同動作。","雙層幕牆是被動式設計，完工後不需要控制系統試運轉。","腔體溫度只要量一個點就能代表整個腔體。"],"optionsEn":["A double-skin façade has to be operated: damper positions, blind angles, inner windows and HVAC must act together according to irradiance, outdoor temperature, wind speed, rain and cavity temperature.","A double-skin façade is passive, so it needs no control commissioning after completion.","One temperature reading represents the whole cavity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"雙層幕牆是一個需要「操作」的立面：風門開度、百葉角度、內層窗戶與空調系統必須依日射、室外溫度、風速、雨量與腔體溫度協同動作。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A double-skin façade has to be operated: damper positions, blind angles, inner windows and HVAC must act together according to irradiance, outdoor temperature, wind speed, rain and cavity temperature. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b089-v13-22","title":"控制系統整合與試運轉：定量估算","titleEn":"Control-system integration and commissioning: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「風門百葉控制點」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Damper and blind control points” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：60 層、每層 40 個開間，每開間 2 個風門與 1 個百葉馬達：致動器 60×40×3 = 7,200 個。若試運轉每日完成 150 個點的逐點測試，需 7,200/150 = 48 個工作天；若每點須加做一次功能測試，約需 96 天。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With 60 floors, 40 bays per floor and 2 dampers plus 1 blind motor per bay, there are 60×40×3 = 7,200 actuators. At 150 point-to-point tests per day, commissioning takes 7,200/150 = 48 working days; adding one functional test per point brings it to about 96 days. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：試運轉分三層：逐點測試（每個致動器與感測器的接線、方向與回饋）、功能測試（依控制邏輯模擬日射、強風、降雨與火警情境）與季節性測試（夏冬各一次實際運轉後檢討趨勢資料）；每項由試運轉顧問見證並記錄缺失與改正。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Commission in three levels: point-to-point tests of each actuator and sensor's wiring, direction and feedback; functional tests simulating irradiance, high wind, rain and fire-alarm scenarios against the control logic; and seasonal tests reviewing trend data after real operation in summer and winter.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"60 層、每層 40 個開間，每開間 2 個風門與 1 個百葉馬達：致動器 60×40×3 = 7,200 個。若試運轉每日完成 150 個點的逐點測試，需 7,200/150 = 48 個工作天；若每點須加做一次功能測試，約需 96 天。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"With 60 floors, 40 bays per floor and 2 dampers plus 1 blind motor per bay, there are 60×40×3 = 7,200 actuators. At 150 point-to-point tests per day, commissioning takes 7,200/150 = 48 working days; adding one functional test per point brings it to about 96 days. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制系統整合與試運轉」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control-system integration and commissioning\", which statement holds?","options":["腔體位於室內外之間受到保護，不需要定期清潔與檢查。","60 層、每層 40 個開間，每開間 2 個風門與 1 個百葉馬達：致動器 60×40×3 = 7,200 個。","多加一層玻璃一定能減少建築的空調耗能。"],"optionsEn":["The cavity is sheltered between inside and outside, so it needs no regular cleaning or inspection.","With 60 floors, 40 bays per floor and 2 dampers plus 1 blind motor per bay, there are 60×40×3 = 7,200 actuators.","Adding a second layer of glass always reduces air-conditioning energy."],"answer":1,"explanation":"60 層、每層 40 個開間，每開間 2 個風門與 1 個百葉馬達：致動器 60×40×3 = 7,200 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With 60 floors, 40 bays per floor and 2 dampers plus 1 blind motor per bay, there are 60×40×3 = 7,200 actuators. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b089-v13-23","title":"控制系統整合與試運轉：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control-system integration and commissioning: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「風門百葉控制點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Damper and blind control points” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"試運轉分三層：逐點測試（每個致動器與感測器的接線、方向與回饋）、功能測試（依控制邏輯模擬日射、強風、降雨與火警情境）與季節性測試（夏冬各一次實際運轉後檢討趨勢資料）；每項由試運轉顧問見證並記錄缺失與改正。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Commission in three levels: point-to-point tests of each actuator and sensor's wiring, direction and feedback; functional tests simulating irradiance, high wind, rain and fire-alarm scenarios against the control logic; and seasonal tests reviewing trend data after real operation in summer and winter. A commissioning authority witnesses each step and logs defects and corrections. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：控制邏輯應以表格列出每個情境的感測條件、致動器動作、優先順序與手動覆寫的自動回復時間；火警時的腔體狀態必須由防火工程師訂定並納入消防聯動測試，未完成者不得取得使用許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: Tabulate the control logic for each scenario with sensing conditions, actuator actions, priorities and automatic reset time after manual override; the cavity state on fire alarm must be set by the fire engineer and included in fire-system interface testing, without which occupancy should not be granted.","failure":"注意干擾：雨量感測器裝在被遮蔽的位置，降雨時風門仍保持開啟而讓雨水進入腔體；火警時控制系統未把腔體風門切換到預定狀態，煙在腔體內擴散到上方樓層。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A rain sensor mounted in a sheltered spot keeps dampers open during rain so water enters the cavity; on a fire alarm the control system fails to move cavity dampers to their preset state and smoke spreads up the cavity; frequent manual overrides of blinds by occupants leave the system without overall coordination. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"試運轉分三層：逐點測試（每個致動器與感測器的接線、方向與回饋）、功能測試（依控制邏輯模擬日射、強風、降雨與火警情境）與季節性測試（夏冬各一次實際運轉後檢討趨勢資料）；每項由試運轉顧問見證並記錄缺失與改正。","textEn":"Commission in three levels: point-to-point tests of each actuator and sensor's wiring, direction and feedback; functional tests simulating irradiance, high wind, rain and fire-alarm scenarios against the control logic; and seasonal tests reviewing trend data after real operation in summer and winter. A commissioning authority witnesses each step and logs defects and corrections.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"控制邏輯應以表格列出每個情境的感測條件、致動器動作、優先順序與手動覆寫的自動回復時間；火警時的腔體狀態必須由防火工程師訂定並納入消防聯動測試，未完成者不得取得使用許可。","textEn":"Tabulate the control logic for each scenario with sensing conditions, actuator actions, priorities and automatic reset time after manual override; the cavity state on fire alarm must be set by the fire engineer and included in fire-system interface testing, without which occupancy should not be granted.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制系統整合與試運轉」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control-system integration and commissioning\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","外層玻璃有開口，所以幾乎不受風壓，可以用很薄的玻璃。","試運轉分三層：逐點測試（每個致動器與感測器的接線、方向與回饋）、功能測試（依控制邏輯模擬日射、強風、降雨與火警情境）與季節性測試（夏冬各一次實際運轉後檢討趨勢資料）。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Because the outer skin has openings, it sees almost no wind and can use very thin glass.","Commission in three levels: point-to-point tests of each actuator and sensor's wiring, direction and feedback."],"answer":2,"explanation":"試運轉分三層：逐點測試（每個致動器與感測器的接線、方向與回饋）、功能測試（依控制邏輯模擬日射、強風、降雨與火警情境）與季節性測試（夏冬各一次實際運轉後檢討趨勢資料）；每項由試運轉顧問見證並記錄缺失與改正。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Commission in three levels: point-to-point tests of each actuator and sensor's wiring, direction and feedback; functional tests simulating irradiance, high wind, rain and fire-alarm scenarios against the control logic; and seasonal tests reviewing trend data after real operation in summer and winter. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b089-v13-24","title":"控制系統整合與試運轉：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control-system integration and commissioning: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「風門百葉控制點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Damper and blind control points” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"雨量感測器裝在被遮蔽的位置，降雨時風門仍保持開啟而讓雨水進入腔體；火警時控制系統未把腔體風門切換到預定狀態，煙在腔體內擴散到上方樓層。使用者頻繁手動覆寫百葉後，系統失去整體協調。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A rain sensor mounted in a sheltered spot keeps dampers open during rain so water enters the cavity; on a fire alarm the control system fails to move cavity dampers to their preset state and smoke spreads up the cavity; frequent manual overrides of blinds by occupants leave the system without overall coordination. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：控制邏輯若只在設計說明中描述而未經實際試運轉，常出現感測器位置不當、指令衝突或手動覆寫後無法回復等問題，使立面長期停在不利的狀態。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Control logic described in a design report but never commissioned often suffers from poorly sited sensors, conflicting commands or manual overrides that never reset, leaving the façade stuck in an unfavourable state for years.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「雙層幕牆是被動式設計，完工後不需要控制系統試運轉。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A double-skin façade is passive, so it needs no control commissioning after completion.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"雨量感測器裝在被遮蔽的位置，降雨時風門仍保持開啟而讓雨水進入腔體；火警時控制系統未把腔體風門切換到預定狀態，煙在腔體內擴散到上方樓層。使用者頻繁手動覆寫百葉後，系統失去整體協調。","textEn":"A rain sensor mounted in a sheltered spot keeps dampers open during rain so water enters the cavity; on a fire alarm the control system fails to move cavity dampers to their preset state and smoke spreads up the cavity; frequent manual overrides of blinds by occupants leave the system without overall coordination.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制系統整合與試運轉」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control-system integration and commissioning\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["雨量感測器裝在被遮蔽的位置，降雨時風門仍保持開啟而讓雨水進入腔體；火警時控制系統未把腔體風門切換到預定狀態，煙在腔體內擴散到上方樓層。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","腔體溫度只要量一個點就能代表整個腔體。"],"optionsEn":["A rain sensor mounted in a sheltered spot keeps dampers open during rain so water enters the cavity.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","One temperature reading represents the whole cavity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"雨量感測器裝在被遮蔽的位置，降雨時風門仍保持開啟而讓雨水進入腔體；火警時控制系統未把腔體風門切換到預定狀態，煙在腔體內擴散到上方樓層。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A rain sensor mounted in a sheltered spot keeps dampers open during rain so water enters the cavity; on a fire alarm the control system fails to move cavity dampers to their preset state and smoke spreads up the cavity; frequent manual overrides of blinds by occupants leave the system without overall coordination. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b089-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「樣品牆與實建築的熱流量測」與「腔體煙流、防火分隔與消防驗證」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Heat-flow measurement on mock-ups and the real building\" and \"Cavity smoke flow, fire separation and fire-safety verification\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b089-v13-25","title":"樣品牆與實建築的熱流量測：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Heat-flow measurement on mock-ups and the real building: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「腔體溫度與風速量測」如何影響雙層通風幕牆整合的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cavity temperature and air-speed survey” governs force, deformation or durability in “Double-skin ventilated facade integration”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"腔體性能無法只靠計算保證，需要在實尺寸樣品牆或完工建築上量測：在腔體不同高度布設遮光溫度計、風速計與日射計，同時量測內層玻璃表面溫度與通過內層的熱通量。由進出風口的風量與溫差可以算出腔體帶走的熱量，再與吸收的日射熱比較，檢查能量平衡是否閉合；若差異很大，代表量測位置、百葉吸收率或滲漏假設有問題。這些資料也是校正控制邏輯與能耗模型的基礎。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「腔體溫度與風速量測」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cavity performance cannot be guaranteed by calculation alone; it must be measured on a full-size mock-up or the completed building. Shielded thermometers, anemometers and pyranometers are placed at several heights in the cavity, while inner-glass surface temperature and heat flux through the inner skin are measured. Airflow and temperature difference across inlets and outlets give the heat removed by the cavity, which is compared with absorbed solar gain to check whether the energy balance closes; a large discrepancy points to problems with sensor positions, blind absorptance or leakage assumptions. These data also form the basis for tuning control logic and energy models. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Cavity temperature and air-speed survey” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：量測風量 0.25 m³/s、進出風口溫差 9 K：帶走熱量 Q = ρ·cp·V·ΔT = 1,206×0.25×9 ≈ 2,714 W；與第一步估算的對流熱 2,268 W 相比高約 (2,714 − 2,268)/2,268 ≈ 20%，表示實際日射或百葉吸收率高於假設，或有室內空氣滲入腔體。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With a measured airflow of 0.25 m³/s and a 9 K inlet-to-outlet difference, the heat removed is Q = ρ·cp·V·ΔT = 1,206×0.25×9 ≈ 2,714 W; compared with the 2,268 W of convected heat estimated earlier it is about (2,714 − 2,268)/2,268 ≈ 20% higher, suggesting irradiance or blind absorptance above the assumption, or room air leaking into the cavity.","failure":"常見誤解：「腔體溫度只要量一個點就能代表整個腔體。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One temperature reading represents the whole cavity.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「腔體溫度與風速量測」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Cavity temperature and air-speed survey”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-25-k1","title":"樣品牆與實建築的熱流量測","titleEn":"Heat-flow measurement on mock-ups and the real building","text":"腔體性能無法只靠計算保證，需要在實尺寸樣品牆或完工建築上量測：在腔體不同高度布設遮光溫度計、風速計與日射計，同時量測內層玻璃表面溫度與通過內層的熱通量。由進出風口的風量與溫差可以算出腔體帶走的熱量，再與吸收的日射熱比較，檢查能量平衡是否閉合；若差異很大，代表量測位置、百葉吸收率或滲漏假設有問題。","textEn":"Cavity performance cannot be guaranteed by calculation alone; it must be measured on a full-size mock-up or the completed building. Shielded thermometers, anemometers and pyranometers are placed at several heights in the cavity, while inner-glass surface temperature and heat flux through the inner skin are measured.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：腔體溫度只要量一個點就能代表整個腔體。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One temperature reading represents the whole cavity. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「樣品牆與實建築的熱流量測」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Heat-flow measurement on mock-ups and the real building\" is correct?","options":["腔體溫度只要量一個點就能代表整個腔體。","腔體性能無法只靠計算保證，需要在實尺寸樣品牆或完工建築上量測：在腔體不同高度布設遮光溫度計、風速計與日射計，同時量測內層玻璃表面溫度與通過內層的熱通量。","雙層幕牆的外層玻璃可以擋住火焰，所以腔體不需要防火設計。"],"optionsEn":["One temperature reading represents the whole cavity.","Cavity performance cannot be guaranteed by calculation alone; it must be measured on a full-size mock-up or the completed building.","The outer glass of a double skin stops flames, so the cavity needs no fire design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"腔體性能無法只靠計算保證，需要在實尺寸樣品牆或完工建築上量測：在腔體不同高度布設遮光溫度計、風速計與日射計，同時量測內層玻璃表面溫度與通過內層的熱通量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cavity performance cannot be guaranteed by calculation alone; it must be measured on a full-size mock-up or the completed building. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b089-v13-26","title":"樣品牆與實建築的熱流量測：定量估算","titleEn":"Heat-flow measurement on mock-ups and the real building: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「腔體溫度與風速量測」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cavity temperature and air-speed survey” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：量測風量 0.25 m³/s、進出風口溫差 9 K：帶走熱量 Q = ρ·cp·V·ΔT = 1,206×0.25×9 ≈ 2,714 W；與第一步估算的對流熱 2,268 W 相比高約 (2,714 − 2,268)/2,268 ≈ 20%，表示實際日射或百葉吸收率高於假設，或有室內空氣滲入腔體。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With a measured airflow of 0.25 m³/s and a 9 K inlet-to-outlet difference, the heat removed is Q = ρ·cp·V·ΔT = 1,206×0.25×9 ≈ 2,714 W; compared with the 2,268 W of convected heat estimated earlier it is about (2,714 − 2,268)/2,268 ≈ 20% higher, suggesting irradiance or blind absorptance above the assumption, or room air leaking into the cavity. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測計畫事先規定感測器校正、遮光方式、取樣頻率、量測期間（至少涵蓋晴天與陰天）與能量平衡允許誤差；樣品牆量測結果與模擬比較後，若差異超過預定範圍，須修正模型或細部再決定量產，並保留原始資料供日後重算。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: The measurement plan states sensor calibration, radiation shielding, sampling rate, duration (covering at least clear and overcast days) and the allowable energy-balance error; if mock-up results differ from simulation beyond the agreed range, revise the model or details before production, and keep the raw data for later recalculation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"量測風量 0.25 m³/s、進出風口溫差 9 K：帶走熱量 Q = ρ·cp·V·ΔT = 1,206×0.25×9 ≈ 2,714 W；與第一步估算的對流熱 2,268 W 相比高約 (2,714 − 2,268)/2,268 ≈ 20%，表示實際日射或百葉吸收率高於假設，或有室內空氣滲入腔體。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"With a measured airflow of 0.25 m³/s and a 9 K inlet-to-outlet difference, the heat removed is Q = ρ·cp·V·ΔT = 1,206×0.25×9 ≈ 2,714 W; compared with the 2,268 W of convected heat estimated earlier it is about (2,714 − 2,268)/2,268 ≈ 20% higher, suggesting irradiance or blind absorptance above the assumption, or room air leaking into the cavity. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「樣品牆與實建築的熱流量測」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Heat-flow measurement on mock-ups and the real building\", which statement holds?","options":["雙層幕牆的節能效果在設計模擬時就已確定，完工後不需要驗證。","雙層幕牆的腔體只要夠高，空氣就一定會由下往上流動。","量測風量 0.25 m³/s、進出風口溫差 9 K：帶走熱量 Q = ρ·cp·V·ΔT = 1,206×0.25×9 ≈ 2,714 W。"],"optionsEn":["The energy savings of a double skin are fixed by the design simulation and need no verification after completion.","If the cavity is tall enough, air will always flow upward through it.","With a measured airflow of 0.25 m³/s and a 9 K inlet-to-outlet difference, the heat removed is Q = ρ·cp·V·ΔT = 1,206×0.25×9 ≈ 2,714 W."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測風量 0.25 m³/s、進出風口溫差 9 K：帶走熱量 Q = ρ·cp·V·ΔT = 1,206×0.25×9 ≈ 2,714 W；與第一步估算的對流熱 2,268 W 相比高約 (2,714 − 2,268)/2,268 ≈ 20%，表示實際日射或百葉吸收率高於假設，或有室內空氣滲入腔體。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With a measured airflow of 0.25 m³/s and a 9 K inlet-to-outlet difference, the heat removed is Q = ρ·cp·V·ΔT = 1,206×0.25×9 ≈ 2,714 W; compared with the 2,268 W of convected heat estimated earlier it is about (2,714 − 2,268)/2,268 ≈ 20% higher, suggesting irradiance or blind absorptance above the assumption, or room air leaking into the cavity. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b089-v13-27","title":"樣品牆與實建築的熱流量測：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Heat-flow measurement on mock-ups and the real building: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「腔體溫度與風速量測」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cavity temperature and air-speed survey” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測計畫事先規定感測器校正、遮光方式、取樣頻率、量測期間（至少涵蓋晴天與陰天）與能量平衡允許誤差；樣品牆量測結果與模擬比較後，若差異超過預定範圍，須修正模型或細部再決定量產，並保留原始資料供日後重算。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"The measurement plan states sensor calibration, radiation shielding, sampling rate, duration (covering at least clear and overcast days) and the allowable energy-balance error; if mock-up results differ from simulation beyond the agreed range, revise the model or details before production, and keep the raw data for later recalculation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：完工後至少保留一個代表性開間的永久量測點，並把腔體溫度、風門與百葉狀態納入建築自動化系統的趨勢紀錄；第一年夏冬季的資料要由設計團隊檢討並調整控制參數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Keep permanent sensors in at least one representative bay after completion and log cavity temperature, damper and blind states as trends in the building-automation system; the design team should review the first summer and winter of data and adjust control parameters.","failure":"注意干擾：溫度計未加遮光，陽光直射使讀值偏高數度，誤判腔體過熱而增加不必要的機械通風；量測只在陰天進行，無法發現夏季晴天的停滯問題，完工後才在最熱的月份出現大量抱怨。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unshielded thermometers read several degrees high in direct sun, falsely indicating overheating and prompting unnecessary mechanical ventilation; measuring only on overcast days misses the clear-sky summer stagnation problem, which surfaces as a flood of complaints in the hottest month after completion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測計畫事先規定感測器校正、遮光方式、取樣頻率、量測期間（至少涵蓋晴天與陰天）與能量平衡允許誤差；樣品牆量測結果與模擬比較後，若差異超過預定範圍，須修正模型或細部再決定量產，並保留原始資料供日後重算。","textEn":"The measurement plan states sensor calibration, radiation shielding, sampling rate, duration (covering at least clear and overcast days) and the allowable energy-balance error; if mock-up results differ from simulation beyond the agreed range, revise the model or details before production, and keep the raw data for later recalculation.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"完工後至少保留一個代表性開間的永久量測點，並把腔體溫度、風門與百葉狀態納入建築自動化系統的趨勢紀錄；第一年夏冬季的資料要由設計團隊檢討並調整控制參數。","textEn":"Keep permanent sensors in at least one representative bay after completion and log cavity temperature, damper and blind states as trends in the building-automation system; the design team should review the first summer and winter of data and adjust control parameters.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「樣品牆與實建築的熱流量測」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Heat-flow measurement on mock-ups and the real building\"?","options":["量測計畫事先規定感測器校正、遮光方式、取樣頻率、量測期間（至少涵蓋晴天與陰天）與能量平衡允許誤差。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","腔體開口只要外觀上夠大，通風量就足夠。"],"optionsEn":["The measurement plan states sensor calibration, radiation shielding, sampling rate, duration (covering at least clear and overcast days) and the allowable energy-balance error.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","If cavity openings look large enough, the airflow will be sufficient."],"answer":0,"explanation":"量測計畫事先規定感測器校正、遮光方式、取樣頻率、量測期間（至少涵蓋晴天與陰天）與能量平衡允許誤差；樣品牆量測結果與模擬比較後，若差異超過預定範圍，須修正模型或細部再決定量產，並保留原始資料供日後重算。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"The measurement plan states sensor calibration, radiation shielding, sampling rate, duration (covering at least clear and overcast days) and the allowable energy-balance error; if mock-up results differ from simulation beyond the agreed range, revise the model or details before production, and keep the raw data for later recalculation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b089-v13-28","title":"樣品牆與實建築的熱流量測：失效診斷","titleEn":"Heat-flow measurement on mock-ups and the real building: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「腔體溫度與風速量測」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cavity temperature and air-speed survey” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"溫度計未加遮光，陽光直射使讀值偏高數度，誤判腔體過熱而增加不必要的機械通風；量測只在陰天進行，無法發現夏季晴天的停滯問題，完工後才在最熱的月份出現大量抱怨。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unshielded thermometers read several degrees high in direct sun, falsely indicating overheating and prompting unnecessary mechanical ventilation; measuring only on overcast days misses the clear-sky summer stagnation problem, which surfaces as a flood of complaints in the hottest month after completion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這些資料也是校正控制邏輯與能耗模型的基礎。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: These data also form the basis for tuning control logic and energy models.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「腔體溫度只要量一個點就能代表整個腔體。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One temperature reading represents the whole cavity.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"溫度計未加遮光，陽光直射使讀值偏高數度，誤判腔體過熱而增加不必要的機械通風；量測只在陰天進行，無法發現夏季晴天的停滯問題，完工後才在最熱的月份出現大量抱怨。","textEn":"Unshielded thermometers read several degrees high in direct sun, falsely indicating overheating and prompting unnecessary mechanical ventilation; measuring only on overcast days misses the clear-sky summer stagnation problem, which surfaces as a flood of complaints in the hottest month after completion.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「樣品牆與實建築的熱流量測」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Heat-flow measurement on mock-ups and the real building\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","溫度計未加遮光，陽光直射使讀值偏高數度，誤判腔體過熱而增加不必要的機械通風；量測只在陰天進行，無法發現夏季晴天的停滯問題，完工後才在最熱的月份出現大量抱怨。","雙層幕牆的外層玻璃可以擋住火焰，所以腔體不需要防火設計。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Unshielded thermometers read several degrees high in direct sun, falsely indicating overheating and prompting unnecessary mechanical ventilation.","The outer glass of a double skin stops flames, so the cavity needs no fire design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"溫度計未加遮光，陽光直射使讀值偏高數度，誤判腔體過熱而增加不必要的機械通風；量測只在陰天進行，無法發現夏季晴天的停滯問題，完工後才在最熱的月份出現大量抱怨。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unshielded thermometers read several degrees high in direct sun, falsely indicating overheating and prompting unnecessary mechanical ventilation; measuring only on overcast days misses the clear-sky summer stagnation problem, which surfaces as a flood of complaints in the hottest month after completion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b089-v13-29","title":"腔體煙流、防火分隔與消防驗證：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Cavity smoke flow, fire separation and fire-safety verification: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「腔體煙控與防火分隔」如何影響雙層通風幕牆整合的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cavity smoke control and fire separation” governs force, deformation or durability in “Double-skin ventilated facade integration”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"雙層幕牆的腔體可能成為火與煙的垂直通道：下層火災破窗後，熱煙進入腔體，被浮力推升並從上層開啟的窗戶或風門回到室內；外層玻璃也可能把火焰反射或約束在腔體內，使上層內層玻璃承受更高的熱暴露。因此防火策略常包括每層或數層的水平分隔、火警時關閉或開啟特定風門、腔體內灑水或耐火玻璃，以及以煙控模擬驗證。這些措施必須與建築的消防分區與避難策略一致。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「腔體煙控與防火分隔」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A double-skin cavity can become a vertical path for fire and smoke: after a fire breaks the windows of a lower floor, hot smoke enters the cavity, is driven upward by buoyancy and re-enters upper floors through open windows or dampers; the outer glass may also reflect or confine flames in the cavity, increasing the heat exposure of inner glazing above. Fire strategies therefore include horizontal divisions at every floor or every few floors, closing or opening particular dampers on alarm, sprinklers or fire-resistant glass in the cavity, and verification by smoke modelling, all consistent with the building's compartmentation and evacuation strategy. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Cavity smoke control and fire separation” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：熱煙在 6 層高（21.6 m）連通腔體中的浮力壓差 ΔP = ρ_a·g·h·(1 − T_a/T_s)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The buoyancy pressure of hot smoke in a six-storey (21.6 m) connected cavity is ΔP = ρ_a·g·h·(1 − T_a/T_s).","failure":"常見誤解：「雙層幕牆的外層玻璃可以擋住火焰，所以腔體不需要防火設計。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The outer glass of a double skin stops flames, so the cavity needs no fire design.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「腔體煙控與防火分隔」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Cavity smoke control and fire separation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-29-k1","title":"腔體煙流、防火分隔與消防驗證","titleEn":"Cavity smoke flow, fire separation and fire-safety verification","text":"雙層幕牆的腔體可能成為火與煙的垂直通道：下層火災破窗後，熱煙進入腔體，被浮力推升並從上層開啟的窗戶或風門回到室內；外層玻璃也可能把火焰反射或約束在腔體內，使上層內層玻璃承受更高的熱暴露。因此防火策略常包括每層或數層的水平分隔、火警時關閉或開啟特定風門、腔體內灑水或耐火玻璃，以及以煙控模擬驗證。","textEn":"A double-skin cavity can become a vertical path for fire and smoke: after a fire breaks the windows of a lower floor, hot smoke enters the cavity, is driven upward by buoyancy and re-enters upper floors through open windows or dampers; the outer glass may also reflect or confine flames in the cavity, increasing the heat exposure of inner glazing above. Fire strategies therefore include horizontal divisions at every floor or every few floors, closing or opening particular dampers on alarm, sprinklers or fire-resistant glass in the cavity, and verification by smoke modelling, all consistent with the building's compartmentation and evacuation strategy.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：雙層幕牆的外層玻璃可以擋住火焰，所以腔體不需要防火設計。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The outer glass of a double skin stops flames, so the cavity needs no fire design. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「腔體煙流、防火分隔與消防驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cavity smoke flow, fire separation and fire-safety verification\" is correct?","options":["雙層幕牆的外層玻璃可以擋住火焰，所以腔體不需要防火設計。","腔體位於室內外之間受到保護，不需要定期清潔與檢查。","雙層幕牆的腔體可能成為火與煙的垂直通道：下層火災破窗後，熱煙進入腔體，被浮力推升並從上層開啟的窗戶或風門回到室內。"],"optionsEn":["The outer glass of a double skin stops flames, so the cavity needs no fire design.","The cavity is sheltered between inside and outside, so it needs no regular cleaning or inspection.","A double-skin cavity can become a vertical path for fire and smoke: after a fire breaks the windows of a lower floor, hot smoke enters the cavity, is driven upward by buoyancy and re-enters upper floors through open windows or dampers."],"answer":2,"explanation":"雙層幕牆的腔體可能成為火與煙的垂直通道：下層火災破窗後，熱煙進入腔體，被浮力推升並從上層開啟的窗戶或風門回到室內；外層玻璃也可能把火焰反射或約束在腔體內，使上層內層玻璃承受更高的熱暴露。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A double-skin cavity can become a vertical path for fire and smoke: after a fire breaks the windows of a lower floor, hot smoke enters the cavity, is driven upward by buoyancy and re-enters upper floors through open windows or dampers; the outer glass may also reflect or confine flames in the cavity, increasing the heat exposure of inner glazing above. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b089-v13-30","title":"腔體煙流、防火分隔與消防驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Cavity smoke flow, fire separation and fire-safety verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「腔體煙控與防火分隔」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cavity smoke control and fire separation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：熱煙在 6 層高（21.6 m）連通腔體中的浮力壓差 ΔP = ρ_a·g·h·(1 − T_a/T_s)。T_a = 293 K、煙溫 T_s = 493 K（比環境高 200 K）：ΔP = 1.2×9.81×21.6×(1 − 293/493) ≈ 103 Pa，遠大於一般樓梯加壓的數十帕，足以把煙推進上層開口。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The buoyancy pressure of hot smoke in a six-storey (21.6 m) connected cavity is ΔP = ρ_a·g·h·(1 − T_a/T_s). With T_a = 293 K and smoke at T_s = 493 K, 200 K above ambient: ΔP = 1.2×9.81×21.6×(1 − 293/493) ≈ 103 Pa, far above the few tens of pascals of typical stair pressurisation and enough to push smoke into openings above. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：由防火工程師以計算流體力學煙控模擬檢查各火災情境下腔體與上層樓層的煙溫、能見度與可用避難時間；現場驗證水平分隔的耐火構造、腔體灑水的覆蓋與排水，並在消防聯動測試中確認火警時每個腔體風門移到預定位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Have the fire engineer run CFD smoke simulations of each fire scenario, checking smoke temperature, visibility and available evacuation time in the cavity and upper floors; on site verify the fire-resisting construction of horizontal divisions and the coverage and drainage of any cavity sprinklers, and confirm in fire-interface testing that every cavity damper moves to its preset position on alarm.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"熱煙在 6 層高（21.6 m）連通腔體中的浮力壓差 ΔP = ρ_a·g·h·(1 − T_a/T_s)。T_a = 293 K、煙溫 T_s = 493 K（比環境高 200 K）：ΔP = 1.2×9.81×21.6×(1 − 293/493) ≈ 103 Pa，遠大於一般樓梯加壓的數十帕，足以把煙推進上層開口。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"The buoyancy pressure of hot smoke in a six-storey (21.6 m) connected cavity is ΔP = ρ_a·g·h·(1 − T_a/T_s). With T_a = 293 K and smoke at T_s = 493 K, 200 K above ambient: ΔP = 1.2×9.81×21.6×(1 − 293/493) ≈ 103 Pa, far above the few tens of pascals of typical stair pressurisation and enough to push smoke into openings above. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「腔體煙流、防火分隔與消防驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cavity smoke flow, fire separation and fire-safety verification\", which statement holds?","options":["熱煙在 6 層高（21.6 m）連通腔體中的浮力壓差 ΔP = ρ_a·g·h·(1 − T_a/T_s)。","多加一層玻璃一定能減少建築的空調耗能。","外層玻璃有開口，所以幾乎不受風壓，可以用很薄的玻璃。"],"optionsEn":["The buoyancy pressure of hot smoke in a six-storey (21.6 m) connected cavity is ΔP = ρ_a·g·h·(1 − T_a/T_s).","Adding a second layer of glass always reduces air-conditioning energy.","Because the outer skin has openings, it sees almost no wind and can use very thin glass."],"answer":0,"explanation":"熱煙在 6 層高（21.6 m）連通腔體中的浮力壓差 ΔP = ρ_a·g·h·(1 − T_a/T_s)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The buoyancy pressure of hot smoke in a six-storey (21.6 m) connected cavity is ΔP = ρ_a·g·h·(1 − T_a/T_s). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b089-v13-31","title":"腔體煙流、防火分隔與消防驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cavity smoke flow, fire separation and fire-safety verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「腔體煙控與防火分隔」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cavity smoke control and fire separation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"由防火工程師以計算流體力學煙控模擬檢查各火災情境下腔體與上層樓層的煙溫、能見度與可用避難時間；現場驗證水平分隔的耐火構造、腔體灑水的覆蓋與排水，並在消防聯動測試中確認火警時每個腔體風門移到預定位置。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Have the fire engineer run CFD smoke simulations of each fire scenario, checking smoke temperature, visibility and available evacuation time in the cavity and upper floors; on site verify the fire-resisting construction of horizontal divisions and the coverage and drainage of any cavity sprinklers, and confirm in fire-interface testing that every cavity damper moves to its preset position on alarm. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：雙層幕牆的防火策略須在設計初期由防火工程師主導，與帷幕牆形式一起決定，並送主管建築與消防機關審查；竣工後任何穿越或改動水平分隔、腔體風門的工程，都須經防火工程師評估。","observationEn":"Site practice: The fire strategy for a double-skin façade must be led by the fire engineer from early design, decided together with the façade type and reviewed by the building and fire authorities; after completion any work that penetrates or alters horizontal divisions or cavity dampers needs the fire engineer's assessment.","failure":"注意干擾：多樓層連通腔體未設任何分隔，下層辦公室火災的煙在數分鐘內進入上方多層，避難時間遠低於設計假設；改裝時移除或穿越水平分隔而未修復，原本合格的防火策略悄悄失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A multi-storey cavity without any division lets smoke from an office fire below reach several floors above within minutes, far less than the assumed evacuation time; removing or penetrating horizontal divisions during later alterations without repair silently defeats a previously compliant strategy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"由防火工程師以計算流體力學煙控模擬檢查各火災情境下腔體與上層樓層的煙溫、能見度與可用避難時間；現場驗證水平分隔的耐火構造、腔體灑水的覆蓋與排水，並在消防聯動測試中確認火警時每個腔體風門移到預定位置。","textEn":"Have the fire engineer run CFD smoke simulations of each fire scenario, checking smoke temperature, visibility and available evacuation time in the cavity and upper floors; on site verify the fire-resisting construction of horizontal divisions and the coverage and drainage of any cavity sprinklers, and confirm in fire-interface testing that every cavity damper moves to its preset position on alarm.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"雙層幕牆的防火策略須在設計初期由防火工程師主導，與帷幕牆形式一起決定，並送主管建築與消防機關審查；竣工後任何穿越或改動水平分隔、腔體風門的工程，都須經防火工程師評估。","textEn":"The fire strategy for a double-skin façade must be led by the fire engineer from early design, decided together with the façade type and reviewed by the building and fire authorities; after completion any work that penetrates or alters horizontal divisions or cavity dampers needs the fire engineer's assessment.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「腔體煙流、防火分隔與消防驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cavity smoke flow, fire separation and fire-safety verification\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","由防火工程師以計算流體力學煙控模擬檢查各火災情境下腔體與上層樓層的煙溫、能見度與可用避難時間。","雙層幕牆只是把一般帷幕牆多做一層，施工程序不需要改變。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Have the fire engineer run CFD smoke simulations of each fire scenario, checking smoke temperature, visibility and available evacuation time in the cavity and upper floors.","A double-skin façade is just an ordinary curtain wall with one more layer, so the construction process need not change."],"answer":1,"explanation":"由防火工程師以計算流體力學煙控模擬檢查各火災情境下腔體與上層樓層的煙溫、能見度與可用避難時間；現場驗證水平分隔的耐火構造、腔體灑水的覆蓋與排水，並在消防聯動測試中確認火警時每個腔體風門移到預定位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Have the fire engineer run CFD smoke simulations of each fire scenario, checking smoke temperature, visibility and available evacuation time in the cavity and upper floors; on site verify the fire-resisting construction of horizontal divisions and the coverage and drainage of any cavity sprinklers, and confirm in fire-interface testing that every cavity damper moves to its preset position on alarm. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b089-v13-32","title":"腔體煙流、防火分隔與消防驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cavity smoke flow, fire separation and fire-safety verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「腔體煙控與防火分隔」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cavity smoke control and fire separation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"多樓層連通腔體未設任何分隔，下層辦公室火災的煙在數分鐘內進入上方多層，避難時間遠低於設計假設；改裝時移除或穿越水平分隔而未修復，原本合格的防火策略悄悄失效。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A multi-storey cavity without any division lets smoke from an office fire below reach several floors above within minutes, far less than the assumed evacuation time; removing or penetrating horizontal divisions during later alterations without repair silently defeats a previously compliant strategy. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這些措施必須與建築的消防分區與避難策略一致。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Fire strategies therefore include horizontal divisions at every floor or every few floors, closing or opening particular dampers on alarm, sprinklers or fire-resistant glass in the cavity, and verification by smoke modelling, all consistent with the building's compartmentation and evacuation strategy.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「雙層幕牆的外層玻璃可以擋住火焰，所以腔體不需要防火設計。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The outer glass of a double skin stops flames, so the cavity needs no fire design.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"多樓層連通腔體未設任何分隔，下層辦公室火災的煙在數分鐘內進入上方多層，避難時間遠低於設計假設；改裝時移除或穿越水平分隔而未修復，原本合格的防火策略悄悄失效。","textEn":"A multi-storey cavity without any division lets smoke from an office fire below reach several floors above within minutes, far less than the assumed evacuation time; removing or penetrating horizontal divisions during later alterations without repair silently defeats a previously compliant strategy.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「腔體煙流、防火分隔與消防驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cavity smoke flow, fire separation and fire-safety verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","腔體位於室內外之間受到保護，不需要定期清潔與檢查。","多樓層連通腔體未設任何分隔，下層辦公室火災的煙在數分鐘內進入上方多層，避難時間遠低於設計假設；改裝時移除或穿越水平分隔而未修復，原本合格的防火策略悄悄失效。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The cavity is sheltered between inside and outside, so it needs no regular cleaning or inspection.","A multi-storey cavity without any division lets smoke from an office fire below reach several floors above within minutes, far less than the assumed evacuation time."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多樓層連通腔體未設任何分隔，下層辦公室火災的煙在數分鐘內進入上方多層，避難時間遠低於設計假設；改裝時移除或穿越水平分隔而未修復，原本合格的防火策略悄悄失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A multi-storey cavity without any division lets smoke from an office fire below reach several floors above within minutes, far less than the assumed evacuation time; removing or penetrating horizontal divisions during later alterations without repair silently defeats a previously compliant strategy. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b089-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「清潔、結露與長期維護」與「實測性能驗證與竣工交接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cleaning, condensation and long-term maintenance\" and \"Measured performance verification and handover\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b089-v13-33","title":"清潔、結露與長期維護：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Cleaning, condensation and long-term maintenance: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「腔體清潔與結露」如何影響雙層通風幕牆整合的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cavity cleaning and condensation” governs force, deformation or durability in “Double-skin ventilated facade integration”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"雙層幕牆有四個玻璃面需要清潔：外層兩面與內層兩面，其中腔體內的兩面只能由檢修走道或可開啟的外層進入。腔體還會累積灰塵、昆蟲與鳥類，使百葉與風門卡住、玻璃透光率下降。冬季若室內的潮濕空氣經由內層漏入腔體，碰到接近室外溫度的外層玻璃內側就會結露，長期造成框料腐蝕與汙漬；因此內層應比外層更氣密，腔體則以室外空氣通風，讓腔體的水汽含量接近室外。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「腔體清潔與結露」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A double-skin façade has four glass faces to clean, two on each skin, and the two inside the cavity can only be reached from the walkway or by opening the outer skin. The cavity also collects dust, insects and birds, jamming blinds and dampers and reducing light transmission. In winter, if moist room air leaks through the inner skin into the cavity, it condenses on the inside of the outer glass, which is close to outdoor temperature, corroding frames and leaving stains over time; so the inner skin should be tighter than the outer, and the cavity ventilated with outdoor air so its moisture content stays close to outdoor conditions. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Cavity cleaning and condensation” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：室內 21°C、相對濕度 50% 的露點約 10.2°C；室外 0°C、相對濕度 80% 的露點約 −3.0°C。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Room air at 21°C and 50% relative humidity has a dew point of about 10.2°C; outdoor air at 0°C and 80% has about −3.0°C.","failure":"常見誤解：「腔體位於室內外之間受到保護，不需要定期清潔與檢查。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The cavity is sheltered between inside and outside, so it needs no regular cleaning or inspection.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「腔體清潔與結露」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Cavity cleaning and condensation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-33-k1","title":"清潔、結露與長期維護","titleEn":"Cleaning, condensation and long-term maintenance","text":"雙層幕牆有四個玻璃面需要清潔：外層兩面與內層兩面，其中腔體內的兩面只能由檢修走道或可開啟的外層進入。腔體還會累積灰塵、昆蟲與鳥類，使百葉與風門卡住、玻璃透光率下降。","textEn":"A double-skin façade has four glass faces to clean, two on each skin, and the two inside the cavity can only be reached from the walkway or by opening the outer skin. The cavity also collects dust, insects and birds, jamming blinds and dampers and reducing light transmission.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：腔體位於室內外之間受到保護，不需要定期清潔與檢查。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The cavity is sheltered between inside and outside, so it needs no regular cleaning or inspection. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「清潔、結露與長期維護」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cleaning, condensation and long-term maintenance\" is correct?","options":["雙層幕牆有四個玻璃面需要清潔：外層兩面與內層兩面，其中腔體內的兩面只能由檢修走道或可開啟的外層進入。","腔體位於室內外之間受到保護，不需要定期清潔與檢查。","雙層幕牆的節能效果在設計模擬時就已確定，完工後不需要驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A double-skin façade has four glass faces to clean, two on each skin, and the two inside the cavity can only be reached from the walkway or by opening the outer skin.","The cavity is sheltered between inside and outside, so it needs no regular cleaning or inspection.","The energy savings of a double skin are fixed by the design simulation and need no verification after completion."],"answer":0,"explanation":"雙層幕牆有四個玻璃面需要清潔：外層兩面與內層兩面，其中腔體內的兩面只能由檢修走道或可開啟的外層進入。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A double-skin façade has four glass faces to clean, two on each skin, and the two inside the cavity can only be reached from the walkway or by opening the outer skin. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b089-v13-34","title":"清潔、結露與長期維護：定量估算","titleEn":"Cleaning, condensation and long-term maintenance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「腔體清潔與結露」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cavity cleaning and condensation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：室內 21°C、相對濕度 50% 的露點約 10.2°C；室外 0°C、相對濕度 80% 的露點約 −3.0°C。外層玻璃內側冬夜約 2°C：若腔體空氣接近室外水汽量（露點 −3°C）不會結露；若室內空氣滲入使露點接近 10°C，就會大量結露。立面 10,000 m² 時，需清潔的玻璃面由單層的 20,000 m² 增為 40,000 m²。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Room air at 21°C and 50% relative humidity has a dew point of about 10.2°C; outdoor air at 0°C and 80% has about −3.0°C. With the inside of the outer glass at about 2°C on a winter night, cavity air close to outdoor moisture (dew point −3°C) will not condense, but room air leaking in and lifting the dew point toward 10°C causes heavy condensation. For a 10,000 m² façade, glass faces to clean rise from 20,000 m² for a single skin to 40,000 m². Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：定期檢查腔體內的結露痕跡、框料腐蝕、百葉與風門動作、防蟲網堵塞與玻璃透光；以氣密試驗確認內層比外層更氣密；冬季以溫濕度紀錄器量測腔體露點與外層玻璃溫度，評估結露時數，並與交接時的基準比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Inspect the cavity periodically for condensation marks, frame corrosion, blind and damper operation, screen clogging and glass transmission; confirm by air-leakage testing that the inner skin is tighter than the outer; in winter log cavity dew point and outer-glass temperature to estimate condensation hours, compared with the handover baseline.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"室內 21°C、相對濕度 50% 的露點約 10.2°C；室外 0°C、相對濕度 80% 的露點約 −3.0°C。外層玻璃內側冬夜約 2°C：若腔體空氣接近室外水汽量（露點 −3°C）不會結露；若室內空氣滲入使露點接近 10°C，就會大量結露。立面 10,000 m² 時，需清潔的玻璃面由單層的 20,000 m² 增為 40,000 m²。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Room air at 21°C and 50% relative humidity has a dew point of about 10.2°C; outdoor air at 0°C and 80% has about −3.0°C. With the inside of the outer glass at about 2°C on a winter night, cavity air close to outdoor moisture (dew point −3°C) will not condense, but room air leaking in and lifting the dew point toward 10°C causes heavy condensation. For a 10,000 m² façade, glass faces to clean rise from 20,000 m² for a single skin to 40,000 m². Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「清潔、結露與長期維護」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cleaning, condensation and long-term maintenance\", which statement holds?","options":["雙層幕牆的腔體只要夠高，空氣就一定會由下往上流動。","室內 21°C、相對濕度 50% 的露點約 10.2°C；室外 0°C、相對濕度 80% 的露點約 −3.0°C。","腔體開口只要外觀上夠大，通風量就足夠。"],"optionsEn":["If the cavity is tall enough, air will always flow upward through it.","Room air at 21°C and 50% relative humidity has a dew point of about 10.2°C; outdoor air at 0°C and 80% has about −3.0°C.","If cavity openings look large enough, the airflow will be sufficient."],"answer":1,"explanation":"室內 21°C、相對濕度 50% 的露點約 10.2°C；室外 0°C、相對濕度 80% 的露點約 −3.0°C。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Room air at 21°C and 50% relative humidity has a dew point of about 10.2°C; outdoor air at 0°C and 80% has about −3.0°C. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b089-v13-35","title":"清潔、結露與長期維護：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cleaning, condensation and long-term maintenance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「腔體清潔與結露」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cavity cleaning and condensation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"定期檢查腔體內的結露痕跡、框料腐蝕、百葉與風門動作、防蟲網堵塞與玻璃透光；以氣密試驗確認內層比外層更氣密；冬季以溫濕度紀錄器量測腔體露點與外層玻璃溫度，評估結露時數，並與交接時的基準比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Inspect the cavity periodically for condensation marks, frame corrosion, blind and damper operation, screen clogging and glass transmission; confirm by air-leakage testing that the inner skin is tighter than the outer; in winter log cavity dew point and outer-glass temperature to estimate condensation hours, compared with the handover baseline. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：維護手冊要列出腔體進入方式、安全措施（防墜、通風、照明）、清潔週期、百葉與風門保養與更換程序，以及結露異常的處理方式；腔體進入屬局限或高處作業時，須依工作許可制度核准。","observationEn":"Site practice: The maintenance manual must state how to enter the cavity, safety measures (fall protection, ventilation, lighting), cleaning intervals, blind and damper servicing and replacement, and what to do about abnormal condensation; where cavity entry is confined-space or work at height, it requires approval under a permit-to-work system.","failure":"注意干擾：內層幕牆氣密不良、腔體又以室內排氣通風，冬季外層玻璃內側每晚結露，水沿框料流入樓板邊緣；清潔預算只以單層幕牆估算，業主減少腔體清潔次數，數年後百葉卡死、透光率下降而增加照明耗能。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A leaky inner skin combined with cavity ventilation by room exhaust air causes condensation on the outer glass every winter night, with water running along frames to the slab edge; a cleaning budget estimated for a single skin leads the owner to cut cavity cleaning, and within a few years blinds jam and reduced light transmission increases lighting energy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"定期檢查腔體內的結露痕跡、框料腐蝕、百葉與風門動作、防蟲網堵塞與玻璃透光；以氣密試驗確認內層比外層更氣密；冬季以溫濕度紀錄器量測腔體露點與外層玻璃溫度，評估結露時數，並與交接時的基準比較。","textEn":"Inspect the cavity periodically for condensation marks, frame corrosion, blind and damper operation, screen clogging and glass transmission; confirm by air-leakage testing that the inner skin is tighter than the outer; in winter log cavity dew point and outer-glass temperature to estimate condensation hours, compared with the handover baseline.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"維護手冊要列出腔體進入方式、安全措施（防墜、通風、照明）、清潔週期、百葉與風門保養與更換程序，以及結露異常的處理方式；腔體進入屬局限或高處作業時，須依工作許可制度核准。","textEn":"The maintenance manual must state how to enter the cavity, safety measures (fall protection, ventilation, lighting), cleaning intervals, blind and damper servicing and replacement, and what to do about abnormal condensation; where cavity entry is confined-space or work at height, it requires approval under a permit-to-work system.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「清潔、結露與長期維護」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cleaning, condensation and long-term maintenance\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","雙層幕牆是被動式設計，完工後不需要控制系統試運轉。","定期檢查腔體內的結露痕跡、框料腐蝕、百葉與風門動作、防蟲網堵塞與玻璃透光。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A double-skin façade is passive, so it needs no control commissioning after completion.","Inspect the cavity periodically for condensation marks, frame corrosion, blind and damper operation, screen clogging and glass transmission."],"answer":2,"explanation":"定期檢查腔體內的結露痕跡、框料腐蝕、百葉與風門動作、防蟲網堵塞與玻璃透光；以氣密試驗確認內層比外層更氣密；冬季以溫濕度紀錄器量測腔體露點與外層玻璃溫度，評估結露時數，並與交接時的基準比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Inspect the cavity periodically for condensation marks, frame corrosion, blind and damper operation, screen clogging and glass transmission; confirm by air-leakage testing that the inner skin is tighter than the outer; in winter log cavity dew point and outer-glass temperature to estimate condensation hours, compared with the handover baseline. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b089-v13-36","title":"清潔、結露與長期維護：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cleaning, condensation and long-term maintenance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「腔體清潔與結露」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cavity cleaning and condensation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"內層幕牆氣密不良、腔體又以室內排氣通風，冬季外層玻璃內側每晚結露，水沿框料流入樓板邊緣；清潔預算只以單層幕牆估算，業主減少腔體清潔次數，數年後百葉卡死、透光率下降而增加照明耗能。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A leaky inner skin combined with cavity ventilation by room exhaust air causes condensation on the outer glass every winter night, with water running along frames to the slab edge; a cleaning budget estimated for a single skin leads the owner to cut cavity cleaning, and within a few years blinds jam and reduced light transmission increases lighting energy. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：冬季若室內的潮濕空氣經由內層漏入腔體，碰到接近室外溫度的外層玻璃內側就會結露，長期造成框料腐蝕與汙漬；因此內層應比外層更氣密，腔體則以室外空氣通風，讓腔體的水汽含量接近室外。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: In winter, if moist room air leaks through the inner skin into the cavity, it condenses on the inside of the outer glass, which is close to outdoor temperature, corroding frames and leaving stains over time; so the inner skin should be tighter than the outer, and the cavity ventilated with outdoor air so its moisture content stays close to outdoor conditions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「腔體位於室內外之間受到保護，不需要定期清潔與檢查。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The cavity is sheltered between inside and outside, so it needs no regular cleaning or inspection.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"內層幕牆氣密不良、腔體又以室內排氣通風，冬季外層玻璃內側每晚結露，水沿框料流入樓板邊緣；清潔預算只以單層幕牆估算，業主減少腔體清潔次數，數年後百葉卡死、透光率下降而增加照明耗能。","textEn":"A leaky inner skin combined with cavity ventilation by room exhaust air causes condensation on the outer glass every winter night, with water running along frames to the slab edge; a cleaning budget estimated for a single skin leads the owner to cut cavity cleaning, and within a few years blinds jam and reduced light transmission increases lighting energy.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「清潔、結露與長期維護」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cleaning, condensation and long-term maintenance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["內層幕牆氣密不良、腔體又以室內排氣通風，冬季外層玻璃內側每晚結露，水沿框料流入樓板邊緣。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","雙層幕牆的節能效果在設計模擬時就已確定，完工後不需要驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A leaky inner skin combined with cavity ventilation by room exhaust air causes condensation on the outer glass every winter night, with water running along frames to the slab edge.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The energy savings of a double skin are fixed by the design simulation and need no verification after completion."],"answer":0,"explanation":"內層幕牆氣密不良、腔體又以室內排氣通風，冬季外層玻璃內側每晚結露，水沿框料流入樓板邊緣；清潔預算只以單層幕牆估算，業主減少腔體清潔次數，數年後百葉卡死、透光率下降而增加照明耗能。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A leaky inner skin combined with cavity ventilation by room exhaust air causes condensation on the outer glass every winter night, with water running along frames to the slab edge; a cleaning budget estimated for a single skin leads the owner to cut cavity cleaning, and within a few years blinds jam and reduced light transmission increases lighting energy. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b089-v13-37","title":"實測性能驗證與竣工交接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Measured performance verification and handover: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「實測能耗與交接紀錄」如何影響雙層通風幕牆整合的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Measured energy and handover records” governs force, deformation or durability in “Double-skin ventilated facade integration”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"雙層幕牆的投資理由通常是節能、舒適、自然通風與隔音，因此交接時不能只交圖面，而要交付可驗證的性能：設計時的能耗與舒適度預測、控制邏輯、試運轉紀錄、量測基準與維護計畫。完工後一到兩年應以實測能耗與趨勢資料比較設計預測，找出控制參數、使用行為或細部的偏差。曼尼托巴水電大樓於 2009 年完工並取得 LEED 白金級，GSW 總部則以西向腔體與可動穿孔金屬遮陽板展現立面與通風一體的設計，這些案例都依賴長期的操作與調整。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「實測能耗與交接紀錄」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The case for a double skin is usually energy, comfort, natural ventilation and acoustics, so handover must deliver verifiable performance, not just drawings: predicted energy and comfort, control logic, commissioning records, measurement baselines and a maintenance plan. One to two years after completion measured energy and trend data should be compared with predictions to find deviations in control parameters, occupant behaviour or details. Manitoba Hydro Place, completed in 2009 with LEED Platinum, and the GSW headquarters, with its west cavity and movable perforated-metal shading panels integrating façade and ventilation, both depend on long-term operation and tuning. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Measured energy and handover records” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：設計預測冷房耗能 80 kWh/m²·年，實測 96 kWh/m²·年，性能落差 (96 − 80)/80 = 20%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Predicted cooling energy is 80 kWh/m²·year and measured is 96 kWh/m²·year, a performance gap of (96 − 80)/80 = 20%.","failure":"常見誤解：「雙層幕牆的節能效果在設計模擬時就已確定，完工後不需要驗證。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The energy savings of a double skin are fixed by the design simulation and need no verification after completion.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「實測能耗與交接紀錄」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Measured energy and handover records”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-37-k1","title":"實測性能驗證與竣工交接","titleEn":"Measured performance verification and handover","text":"雙層幕牆的投資理由通常是節能、舒適、自然通風與隔音，因此交接時不能只交圖面，而要交付可驗證的性能：設計時的能耗與舒適度預測、控制邏輯、試運轉紀錄、量測基準與維護計畫。完工後一到兩年應以實測能耗與趨勢資料比較設計預測，找出控制參數、使用行為或細部的偏差。","textEn":"The case for a double skin is usually energy, comfort, natural ventilation and acoustics, so handover must deliver verifiable performance, not just drawings: predicted energy and comfort, control logic, commissioning records, measurement baselines and a maintenance plan. One to two years after completion measured energy and trend data should be compared with predictions to find deviations in control parameters, occupant behaviour or details.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：雙層幕牆的節能效果在設計模擬時就已確定，完工後不需要驗證。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The energy savings of a double skin are fixed by the design simulation and need no verification after completion. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「實測性能驗證與竣工交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Measured performance verification and handover\" is correct?","options":["雙層幕牆的節能效果在設計模擬時就已確定，完工後不需要驗證。","雙層幕牆的投資理由通常是節能、舒適、自然通風與隔音，因此交接時不能只交圖面，而要交付可驗證的性能：設計時的能耗與舒適度預測、控制邏輯、試運轉紀錄、量測基準與維護計畫。","多加一層玻璃一定能減少建築的空調耗能。"],"optionsEn":["The energy savings of a double skin are fixed by the design simulation and need no verification after completion.","The case for a double skin is usually energy, comfort, natural ventilation and acoustics, so handover must deliver verifiable performance, not just drawings: predicted energy and comfort, control logic, commissioning records, measurement baselines and a maintenance plan.","Adding a second layer of glass always reduces air-conditioning energy."],"answer":1,"explanation":"雙層幕牆的投資理由通常是節能、舒適、自然通風與隔音，因此交接時不能只交圖面，而要交付可驗證的性能：設計時的能耗與舒適度預測、控制邏輯、試運轉紀錄、量測基準與維護計畫。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The case for a double skin is usually energy, comfort, natural ventilation and acoustics, so handover must deliver verifiable performance, not just drawings: predicted energy and comfort, control logic, commissioning records, measurement baselines and a maintenance plan. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b089-v13-38","title":"實測性能驗證與竣工交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Measured performance verification and handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「實測能耗與交接紀錄」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Measured energy and handover records” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：設計預測冷房耗能 80 kWh/m²·年，實測 96 kWh/m²·年，性能落差 (96 − 80)/80 = 20%。若分析顯示其中 12 kWh/m²·年來自百葉控制門檻設得太高，調整後預估回到 84 kWh/m²·年，落差縮小為 5%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Predicted cooling energy is 80 kWh/m²·year and measured is 96 kWh/m²·year, a performance gap of (96 − 80)/80 = 20%. If analysis attributes 12 kWh/m²·year to a blind-control threshold set too high, retuning is predicted to bring consumption back to 84 kWh/m²·year, narrowing the gap to 5%. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：交接後的第一年進行季節性複驗：比較分項電表、腔體溫度與風門百葉趨勢資料與設計預測，訪查使用者舒適度與手動覆寫頻率，提出調整清單並重新試運轉；結果寫入性能報告，作為保固期結束前的驗收依據。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: In the first year after handover carry out seasonal re-verification: compare sub-metered energy and cavity-temperature, damper and blind trends with predictions, survey occupant comfort and override frequency, issue a tuning list and recommission; record the outcome in a performance report used for acceptance before the warranty expires.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"設計預測冷房耗能 80 kWh/m²·年，實測 96 kWh/m²·年，性能落差 (96 − 80)/80 = 20%。若分析顯示其中 12 kWh/m²·年來自百葉控制門檻設得太高，調整後預估回到 84 kWh/m²·年，落差縮小為 5%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Predicted cooling energy is 80 kWh/m²·year and measured is 96 kWh/m²·year, a performance gap of (96 − 80)/80 = 20%. If analysis attributes 12 kWh/m²·year to a blind-control threshold set too high, retuning is predicted to bring consumption back to 84 kWh/m²·year, narrowing the gap to 5%. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「實測性能驗證與竣工交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Measured performance verification and handover\", which statement holds?","options":["外層玻璃有開口，所以幾乎不受風壓，可以用很薄的玻璃。","雙層幕牆只是把一般帷幕牆多做一層，施工程序不需要改變。","設計預測冷房耗能 80 kWh/m²·年，實測 96 kWh/m²·年，性能落差 (96 − 80)/80 = 20%。"],"optionsEn":["Because the outer skin has openings, it sees almost no wind and can use very thin glass.","A double-skin façade is just an ordinary curtain wall with one more layer, so the construction process need not change.","Predicted cooling energy is 80 kWh/m²·year and measured is 96 kWh/m²·year, a performance gap of (96 − 80)/80 = 20%."],"answer":2,"explanation":"設計預測冷房耗能 80 kWh/m²·年，實測 96 kWh/m²·年，性能落差 (96 − 80)/80 = 20%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Predicted cooling energy is 80 kWh/m²·year and measured is 96 kWh/m²·year, a performance gap of (96 − 80)/80 = 20%. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b089-v13-39","title":"實測性能驗證與竣工交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Measured performance verification and handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「實測能耗與交接紀錄」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Measured energy and handover records” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"交接後的第一年進行季節性複驗：比較分項電表、腔體溫度與風門百葉趨勢資料與設計預測，訪查使用者舒適度與手動覆寫頻率，提出調整清單並重新試運轉；結果寫入性能報告，作為保固期結束前的驗收依據。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"In the first year after handover carry out seasonal re-verification: compare sub-metered energy and cavity-temperature, damper and blind trends with predictions, survey occupant comfort and override frequency, issue a tuning list and recommission; record the outcome in a performance report used for acceptance before the warranty expires. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：竣工文件應包含腔體類型與設計準則、控制邏輯表、試運轉與量測紀錄、維護手冊、消防聯動狀態與性能驗證計畫；任何改變控制參數、遮陽或腔體分隔的變更，須經原設計團隊或指定顧問評估並記錄。","observationEn":"Site practice: Completion documents should include cavity type and design criteria, the control-logic table, commissioning and measurement records, the maintenance manual, fire-interface states and the performance-verification plan; any change to control parameters, shading or cavity divisions needs assessment by the original design team or an appointed consultant, and must be recorded.","failure":"注意干擾：交接時沒有控制邏輯說明與量測基準，管理單位為了減少抱怨把百葉與風門全部改為手動，雙層幕牆變成昂貴的單層幕牆；能耗上升也無從判斷原因。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Without control-logic documentation and measurement baselines at handover, building management switches all blinds and dampers to manual to reduce complaints, turning the double skin into an expensive single skin; rising energy then has no traceable cause. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"交接後的第一年進行季節性複驗：比較分項電表、腔體溫度與風門百葉趨勢資料與設計預測，訪查使用者舒適度與手動覆寫頻率，提出調整清單並重新試運轉；結果寫入性能報告，作為保固期結束前的驗收依據。","textEn":"In the first year after handover carry out seasonal re-verification: compare sub-metered energy and cavity-temperature, damper and blind trends with predictions, survey occupant comfort and override frequency, issue a tuning list and recommission; record the outcome in a performance report used for acceptance before the warranty expires.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"竣工文件應包含腔體類型與設計準則、控制邏輯表、試運轉與量測紀錄、維護手冊、消防聯動狀態與性能驗證計畫；任何改變控制參數、遮陽或腔體分隔的變更，須經原設計團隊或指定顧問評估並記錄。","textEn":"Completion documents should include cavity type and design criteria, the control-logic table, commissioning and measurement records, the maintenance manual, fire-interface states and the performance-verification plan; any change to control parameters, shading or cavity divisions needs assessment by the original design team or an appointed consultant, and must be recorded.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「實測性能驗證與竣工交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Measured performance verification and handover\"?","options":["交接後的第一年進行季節性複驗：比較分項電表、腔體溫度與風門百葉趨勢資料與設計預測，訪查使用者舒適度與手動覆寫頻率，提出調整清單並重新試運轉。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","腔體溫度只要量一個點就能代表整個腔體。"],"optionsEn":["In the first year after handover carry out seasonal re-verification: compare sub-metered energy and cavity-temperature, damper and blind trends with predictions, survey occupant comfort and override frequency, issue a tuning list and recommission.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","One temperature reading represents the whole cavity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"交接後的第一年進行季節性複驗：比較分項電表、腔體溫度與風門百葉趨勢資料與設計預測，訪查使用者舒適度與手動覆寫頻率，提出調整清單並重新試運轉；結果寫入性能報告，作為保固期結束前的驗收依據。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"In the first year after handover carry out seasonal re-verification: compare sub-metered energy and cavity-temperature, damper and blind trends with predictions, survey occupant comfort and override frequency, issue a tuning list and recommission; record the outcome in a performance report used for acceptance before the warranty expires. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b089-v13-40","title":"實測性能驗證與竣工交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Measured performance verification and handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b089-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「實測能耗與交接紀錄」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Measured energy and handover records” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"交接時沒有控制邏輯說明與量測基準，管理單位為了減少抱怨把百葉與風門全部改為手動，雙層幕牆變成昂貴的單層幕牆；能耗上升也無從判斷原因。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Without control-logic documentation and measurement baselines at handover, building management switches all blinds and dampers to manual to reduce complaints, turning the double skin into an expensive single skin; rising energy then has no traceable cause. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：曼尼托巴水電大樓於 2009 年完工並取得 LEED 白金級，GSW 總部則以西向腔體與可動穿孔金屬遮陽板展現立面與通風一體的設計，這些案例都依賴長期的操作與調整。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Manitoba Hydro Place, completed in 2009 with LEED Platinum, and the GSW headquarters, with its west cavity and movable perforated-metal shading panels integrating façade and ventilation, both depend on long-term operation and tuning.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「雙層幕牆的節能效果在設計模擬時就已確定，完工後不需要驗證。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The energy savings of a double skin are fixed by the design simulation and need no verification after completion.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b089-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"交接時沒有控制邏輯說明與量測基準，管理單位為了減少抱怨把百葉與風門全部改為手動，雙層幕牆變成昂貴的單層幕牆；能耗上升也無從判斷原因。","textEn":"Without control-logic documentation and measurement baselines at handover, building management switches all blinds and dampers to manual to reduce complaints, turning the double skin into an expensive single skin; rising energy then has no traceable cause.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]},{"id":"b089-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「實測性能驗證與竣工交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Measured performance verification and handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","交接時沒有控制邏輯說明與量測基準，管理單位為了減少抱怨把百葉與風門全部改為手動，雙層幕牆變成昂貴的單層幕牆；能耗上升也無從判斷原因。","多加一層玻璃一定能減少建築的空調耗能。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Without control-logic documentation and measurement baselines at handover, building management switches all blinds and dampers to manual to reduce complaints, turning the double skin into an expensive single skin.","Adding a second layer of glass always reduces air-conditioning energy."],"answer":1,"explanation":"交接時沒有控制邏輯說明與量測基準，管理單位為了減少抱怨把百葉與風門全部改為手動，雙層幕牆變成昂貴的單層幕牆；能耗上升也無從判斷原因。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Without control-logic documentation and measurement baselines at handover, building management switches all blinds and dampers to manual to reduce complaints, turning the double skin into an expensive single skin; rising energy then has no traceable cause. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-kpmb-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-sauerbruch-hutton-gsw","v13s-arup-30-st-mary-axe","v13s-wiki-manitoba-hydro-place","v13s-wiki-30-st-mary-axe"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
